  ["feature.additional-fighting-style.phb2014.fighter.champion.10"]={title="Additional Fighting Style",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\nAt 10th level, you can choose a second option from the Fighting Style class feature."},
  ["feature.additional-fighting-style.xphb2024.fighter.champion.7"]={title="Additional Fighting Style",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 96\n\nYou gain another feats of your choice."},
  ["feature.additional-magical-secrets.phb2014.bard.lore.6"]={title="Additional Magical Secrets",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 54\n\nAt 6th level, you learn two spells of your choice from any class. A spell you choose must be of a level you can cast, as shown on the Bard table, or a cantrip. The chosen spells count as bard spells for you but don't count against the number of bard spells you know."},
  ["feature.additional-maneuvers.phb2014.fighter.battle-master.7"]={title="Additional Maneuvers",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.additional-maneuvers.phb2014.fighter.battle-master.10"]={title="Additional Maneuvers",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.additional-maneuvers.phb2014.fighter.battle-master.15"]={title="Additional Maneuvers",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.additional-rune-known.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.7"]={title="Additional Rune Known",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\n7th-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou learn an additional Rune."},
  ["feature.additional-rune-known.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.10"]={title="Additional Rune Known",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\n10th-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou learn an additional Rune."},
  ["feature.additional-rune-known.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.15"]={title="Additional Rune Known",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\n15th-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou learn an additional Rune."},
  ["feature.additional-superiority-die.phb2014.fighter.battle-master.7"]={title="Additional Superiority Die",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.additional-superiority-die.phb2014.fighter.battle-master.15"]={title="Additional Superiority Die",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feat.adept-of-the-black-robes.dsotdq2014"]={title="Adept of the Black Robes",subtitle="Feat - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\nYou chose the moon Nuitari to influence your magic, and your ambition and loyalty to the Order of the Black Robes have been recognized, granting you these benefits:\n\n• Ambitious Magic You learn one 2nd-level spell of your choice. The spells must be from the enchantment or necromancy school of magic. You can cast this feat's 2nd-level spell without a spell slot, and you must finish a long rest before you can cast it in this way again. You can also cast this spell using spell slots you have of the appropriate level. The spell's spellcasting ability is the one chosen when you gained the DSotDQ feat.\n\n• Life Channel You can channel your life force into the power of your magic. When a creature you can see within 60 feet of you fails a saving throw against a spell that deals damage that you cast, you can expend a number of Hit Dice equal to the level of the spell. Roll the expended Hit Dice and add them together. The damage that the creature takes increases by an amount equal to that total."},
  ["feat.adept-of-the-red-robes.dsotdq2014"]={title="Adept of the Red Robes",subtitle="Feat - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\nYou chose the moon Lunitari to influence your magic, and your dedication to maintaining the balance between all things has been recognized by the Order of the Red Robes, granting you these benefits:\n\n• Insightful Magic You learn one 2nd-level spell of your choice. The spells must be from the illusion or transmutation school of magic. You can cast this feat's 2nd-level spell without a spell slot, and you must finish a long rest before you can cast it in this way again. You can also cast this spell using spell slots you have of the appropriate level. The spell's spellcasting ability is the one chosen when you gained the DSotDQ feat.\n\n• Magical Balance When you make an attack roll or an ability check and roll a 9 or lower on the d20, you can balance fate and treat the roll as a 10. You can balance fate in this way a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},
  ["feat.adept-of-the-white-robes.dsotdq2014"]={title="Adept of the White Robes",subtitle="Feat - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\nYou chose the moon Solinari to influence your magic, and your oath to use magic to make the world a better place has been recognized by the Order of the White Robes, granting you these benefits:\n\n• Protective Magic You learn one 2nd-level spell of your choice. The spells must be from the abjuration or divination school of magic. You can cast this feat's 2nd-level spell without a spell slot, and you must finish a long rest before you can cast it in this way again. You can also cast this spell using spell slots you have of the appropriate level. The spell's spellcasting ability is the one chosen when you gained the DSotDQ feat.\n\n• Protective Ward When you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of you takes damage, you can use your reaction to expend a spell slot and weave protective magic around the target. Roll a number of d6s equal to the level of the spell slot expended and reduce the damage the target takes by the total rolled on those dice + your spellcasting ability modifier."},
  ["feature.adjust-density.egw2014.wizard.graviturgy.2"]={title="Adjust Density",subtitle="Caracteristica - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["item.adjustable-stilts.wdh2014"]={title="Adjustable Stilts",subtitle="Item - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 47\n\nRaridade: unknown\n\nThe stilts take 1 minute to put on or remove. They increase the height of any humanoid wearing them by 2 to 5 feet. Each stilt weighs 8 pounds and is 1 foot long when fully collapsed."},
  ["creature.adult-amethyst-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Adult Amethyst Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 161\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 229 (17d12 + 119)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 14 | CON 25 | INT 20 | WIS 17 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: force, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe both air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (2d10 + 7) piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) force damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h11 (1d8 + 7) slashing damage.\n\nSingularity Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon creates a shining bead of gravitational force in its mouth, then releases the energy in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 20 Strength saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 45 (10d8) force damage, and its speed becomes 0 until the start of the dragon's next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage, and its speed isn't reduced.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe dragon magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe dragon makes one claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nExplosive Crystal (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe dragon spits an amethyst that explodes at a point it can see within 60 feet of it. Each creature within a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must succeed on a 20 Dexterity saving throw or take 13 (3d8) force damage and be knocked prone."},
  ["creature.adult-amonkhet-dragon.psa2014"]={title="Adult Amonkhet Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 8"},
  ["creature.adult-black-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Adult Black Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 88\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 195 (17d12 + 85)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 14 | CON 21 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) acid damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h15 (2d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nAcid Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales acid in a 60-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking 54 (12d8) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 10 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 19 Dexterity saving throw or take 13 (2d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.adult-black-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Adult Black Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 39\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 195 (17d12 + 85)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 14 | CON 21 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 3 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 11, reach 10 ft. h13 (2d6 + 6) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Acid damage.\n\nAcid Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 18, each creature in a 60-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 54 (12d8) Acid damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCloud of Insects\n\ndex 17, one creature the dragon can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 22 (4d10) Poison damage, and the target has XPHB on saving throws to maintain XPHB until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB. The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon can move up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.adult-blue-dracolich.mm2014"]={title="Adult Blue Dracolich",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 84\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / H\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 225 (18d12 + 108)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 10 | CON 23 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\nImunidades: lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dracolich fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe dracolich has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dracolich can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (2d10 + 7) piercing damage plus 5 (1d10) lightning damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d6 + 7) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h16 (2d8 + 7) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dracolich's choice that is within 120 feet of the dracolich and aware of it must succeed on a 18 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dracolich's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dracolich exhales lightning in a 90-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 20 Dexterity saving throw, taking 66 (12d10) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dracolich makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dracolich makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dracolich beats its tattered wings. Each creature within 10 feet of the dracolich must succeed on a 21 Dexterity saving throw or take 14 (2d6 + 7) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. After beating its wings this way, the dracolich can fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.adult-blue-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Adult Blue Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 91\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 225 (18d12 + 108)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 10 | CON 23 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (2d10 + 7) piercing damage plus 5 (1d10) lightning damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d6 + 7) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h16 (2d8 + 7) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales lightning in a 90-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 19 Dexterity saving throw, taking 66 (12d10) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 10 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 20 Dexterity saving throw or take 14 (2d6 + 7) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.adult-blue-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Adult Blue Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 49\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 212 (17d12 + 102)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 10 | CON 23 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB.\n\nRend\n\nm 12, reach 10 ft. h16 (2d8 + 7) Slashing damage plus 5 (1d10) Lightning damage.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 19, each creature in a 90-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 60 (11d10) Lightning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCloaked Flight\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB on itself, and it can fly up to half its XPHB. The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nSonic Boom\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB. The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nTail Swipe\n\nThe dragon makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.adult-brass-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Adult Brass Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 105\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 172 (15d12 + 75)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h15 (2d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Fire Breath\n\n• Sleep Breath\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 10 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 19 Dexterity saving throw or take 13 (2d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.adult-brass-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Adult Brass Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 55\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 172 (15d12 + 75)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of (A) Sleep Breath or (B) Spellcasting to cast XPHB.\n\nRend\n\nm 11, reach 10 ft. h17 (2d10 + 6) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Fire damage.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 18, each creature in a 60-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 45 (10d8) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nSleep Breath\n\ncon 18, each creature in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn, at which point it repeats the save. 2 The target has the XPHB condition for 10 minutes. This effect ends for the target if it takes damage or a creature within 5 feet of it takes an action to wake it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nBlazing Light\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack.\n\nScorching Sands\n\ndex 16, one creature the dragon can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 27 (6d8) Fire damage, and the target's XPHB is halved until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn."},
  ["creature.adult-bronze-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Adult Bronze Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 108\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 212 (17d12 + 102)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 10 | CON 23 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (2d10 + 7) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d6 + 7) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h16 (2d8 + 7) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Lightning Breath\n\n• Repulsion Breath\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically polymorphs into a humanoid or beast that has a challenge rating no higher than its own, or back into its true form. It reverts to its true form if it dies. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying is absorbed or borne by the new form (the dragon's choice).\n\nIn a new form, the dragon retains its alignment, hit points, Hit Dice, ability to speak, proficiencies, Legendary Resistance, lair actions, and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores, as well as this action. Its statistics and capabilities are otherwise replaced by those of the new form, except any class features or legendary actions of that form.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 10 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 20 Dexterity saving throw or take 14 (2d6 + 7) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.adult-bronze-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Adult Bronze Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 59\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 212 (17d12 + 102)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 10 | CON 23 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of (A) Repulsion Breath or (B) Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 12, reach 10 ft. h16 (2d8 + 7) Slashing damage plus 5 (1d10) Lightning damage.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 19, each creature in a 90-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 55 (10d10) Lightning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nRepulsion Breath\n\nstr 19, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target is pushed up to 60 feet straight away from the dragon and has the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nGuiding Light\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version).\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack.\n\nThunderclap\n\ncon 17, each creature in a 20-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point the dragon can see within 90 feet. actSaveFail 10 (3d6) Thunder damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.adult-copper-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Adult Copper Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 184 (16d12 + 80)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 12 | CON 21 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h15 (2d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Acid Breath\n\n• Slowing Breath\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 10 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 19 Dexterity saving throw or take 13 (2d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.adult-copper-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Adult Copper Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 79\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 184 (16d12 + 80)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 12 | CON 21 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of (A) Slowing Breath or (B) Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 4 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 11, reach 10 ft. h17 (2d10 + 6) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Acid damage.\n\nAcid Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 18, each creature in an 60-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 54 (12d8) Acid damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nSlowing Breath\n\ncon 18, each creature in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target can't take Reactions; its XPHB is halved; and it can take either an action or a XPHB on its turn, not both. This effect lasts until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nGiggling Magic\n\ncha 17, one creature the dragon can see within 90 feet. actSaveFail 24 (7d6) Psychic damage. Until the end of its next turn, the target rolls 1d6 whenever it makes an ability check or attack roll and subtracts the number rolled from the XPHB. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nMind Jolt\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 4 version). The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.adult-crystal-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Adult Crystal Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 171\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 172 (15d12 + 75)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 12 | CON 21 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, radiant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) radiant damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nScintillating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a burst of brilliant radiance in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 17 Constitution saving throw, taking 40 (9d8) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The dragon then gains 15 temporary hit points by absorbing a portion of the radiant energy.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe dragon magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe dragon makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nStarlight Strike (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe dragon releases a searing beam of starlight at a creature that it can see within 60 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 17 Dexterity saving throw or take 31 (9d6) radiant damage."},
  ["creature.adult-deep-dragon.fraif2014"]={title="Adult Deep Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 258\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 161 (17d12 + 51)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 16 | WIS 16 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 150 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Undercommon\n\nResistencias: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 9, reach 10 ft. h14 (2d8 + 5) Slashing damage plus 5 (1d10) Poison damage.\n\nNightmare Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nwis 15, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 38 (7d10) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of the dragon's next turn. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShape-Shift\n\nThe dragon shape-shifts into a Small or Medium Humanoid or a Small or Medium Beast, or it returns to its true form. Its game statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack.\n\nSpore Salvo\n\ncon 15, one creature within 30 feet of the dragon that it can see. actSaveFail 13 (3d8) Poison damage, and the target has the XPHB condition. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn."},
  ["creature.adult-deep-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Adult Deep Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 174\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 147 (14d12 + 56)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 16 | WIS 16 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 150 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Undercommon\n\nResistencias: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) piercing damage plus 5 (1d10) poison damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d6 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 17 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses its action to end it.\n\nNightmare Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a cloud of spores in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 16 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 33 (6d10) psychic damage, and it is frightened of the dragon for 1 minute. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage with no additional effects. A frightened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCommanding Spores\n\nThe dragon releases spores around a creature within 30 feet of it that it can see. The target must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or use its reaction to make a melee weapon attack against a random creature within reach. If no creatures are within reach, or the target can't take a reaction, it takes 5 (1d10) psychic damage.\n\nTail\n\nThe dragon makes one Tail attack.\n\nSpore Salvo (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon releases poisonous spores around a creature within 30 feet of it that it can see. The target must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or take 17 (5d6) poison damage and become poisoned for 1 minute. The poisoned creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.adult-emerald-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Adult Emerald Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 196\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 207 (18d12 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 12 | CON 21 | INT 18 | WIS 16 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: fire, psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nShift Perception (1/Day)\n\nThe dragon can cast hallucinatory terrain, requiring no spell components and using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability (spell save 17).\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and can leave a 15-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) psychic damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (1d8 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nDisorienting Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a wave of psychic dissonance in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 18 Intelligence saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 42 (12d6) psychic damage, and until the end of its next turn, when the creature makes an attack roll or an ability check, it must roll a d6 and reduce the total by the number rolled. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage with no additional effects.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe dragon magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe dragon makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nEmerald Embers (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe dragon creates a dancing mote of green flame around a creature it can see within 60 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 17 Dexterity saving throw or take 31 (9d6) fire damage."},
