encies, Legendary Resistance, lair actions, and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores, as well as this action. Its statistics and capabilities are otherwise replaced by those of the new form, except any class features or legendary actions of that form.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 10 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 22 Dexterity saving throw or take 15 (2d6 + 8) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.adult-gold-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Adult Gold Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 145\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 243 (18d12 + 126)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 14 | CON 25 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 24\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of (A) Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version) or (B) Weakening Breath.\n\nRend\n\nm 14, reach 10 ft. h17 (2d8 + 8) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Fire damage.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 21, each creature in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 66 (12d10) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nWeakening Breath\n\nstr 21, each creature that isn't currently affected by this breath in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target has XPHB on Strength-based XPHB and subtracts 3 (1d6) from its damage rolls. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nBanish\n\ncha 21, one creature the dragon can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 10 (3d6) Force damage, and the target has the XPHB condition and is transported to a harmless demiplane until the start of the dragon's next turn, at which point it reappears in an unoccupied space of the dragon's choice within 120 feet of the dragon. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nGuiding Light\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version).\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.adult-green-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Adult Green Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 207 (18d12 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 12 | CON 21 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) poison damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h15 (2d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nPoison Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales poisonous gas in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 18 Constitution saving throw, taking 56 (16d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 10 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 19 Dexterity saving throw or take 13 (2d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.adult-green-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Adult Green Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 153\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 207 (18d12 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 12 | CON 21 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 3 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 11, reach 10 ft. h15 (2d8 + 6) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage.\n\nPoison Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 18, each creature in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 56 (16d6) Poison damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nMind Invasion\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 3 version).\n\nNoxious Miasma\n\ncon 17, each creature in a 20-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point the dragon can see within 90 feet. actSaveFail 7 (2d6) Poison damage, and the target takes a -2 penalty to AC until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.adult-kruthik.mpmm2014"]={title="Adult Kruthik",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 169\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 39 (6d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, climb: 40\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 7 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft., tremorsense 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Kruthik\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe kruthik has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the kruthik's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe kruthik can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and leaves a 5-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe kruthik makes two Stab or Spike attacks.\n\nStab\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nSpike\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.adult-kruthik.mtf2014"]={title="Adult Kruthik",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 39 (6d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, climb: 40\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 7 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft., tremorsense 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Kruthik\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe kruthik has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe kruthik has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the kruthik's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe kruthik can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and leaves a 5-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe kruthik makes two stab attacks or two spike attacks.\n\nStab\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nSpike\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.adult-lunar-dragon.bam2014"]={title="Adult Lunar Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 172 (15d12 + 75)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 12 | CON 20 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 240 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and leaves a 15-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe dragon doesn't require air.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) cold damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a blast of frost in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in the cone must make a 18 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 36 (8d8) cold damage, and its speed is reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage, and its speed isn't reduced.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nPhase (3/Day)\n\nThe dragon becomes partially incorporeal for as long as it maintains concentration on the effect (as if concentration on a spell). While partially incorporeal, the dragon has resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes one Tail attack.\n\nTreacherous Ice\n\nMagical ice covers the ground in a 20-foot radius centered on a point the dragon can see within 120 feet of itself. The ice, which is difficult terrain for all creatures except lunar dragons, lasts for 10 minutes or until the dragon uses this legendary action again."},
  ["creature.adult-moonstone-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Adult Moonstone Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 195 (17d12 + 85)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 18 | CON 20 | INT 22 | WIS 20 | CHA 23\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Elvish, Gnomish, Sylvan\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) radiant damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 18 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nBreath Weapon {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons:\n\n• Dream Breath The dragon exhales mist in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 18 Constitution saving throw or fall unconscious for 10 minutes. This effect ends for a creature if the creature takes damage or someone uses an action to wake it.\n\n• Moonlight Breath The dragon exhales a beam of moonlight in a 90-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that area must make a 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking 49 (9d10) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTail\n\nThe dragon makes one Tail attack.\n\nCast a Spell (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting."},
  ["creature.adult-oblex.mpmm2014"]={title="Adult Oblex",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 198\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: ooze / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 75 (10d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 19 | CON 16 | INT 19 | WIS 12 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this distance)\n\nIdiomas: Common plus two more languages\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmorphous\n\nThe oblex can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.\n\nAversion to Fire\n\nIf the oblex takes fire damage, it has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks until the end of its next turn.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe oblex doesn't require sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe oblex makes two pseudopod attacks, and it uses Eat Memories.\n\nPseudopod\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) psychic damage.\n\nEat Memories\n\nThe oblex targets one creature it can see within 5 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or take 18 (4d8) psychic damage and become memory drained until it finishes a short or long rest or until it benefits from the greater restoration or heal spell. Constructs, Oozes, Plants, and Undead succeed on the save automatically.\n\nWhile memory drained, the target must roll a d4 and subtract the number rolled from its ability checks and attack rolls. Each time the target is memory drained beyond the first, the die size increases by one: the d4 becomes a d6, the d6 becomes a d8, and so on until the die becomes a d20, at which point the target becomes unconscious for 1 hour. The effect then ends.\n\nThe oblex learns all the languages a memory-drained target knows and gains all its skill proficiencies.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nSulfurous Impersonation\n\nThe oblex extrudes a piece of itself that assumes the appearance of one Medium or smaller creature whose memories it has stolen. This simulacrum appears, feels, and sounds exactly like the creature it impersonates, though it smells faintly of sulfur. The oblex can impersonate 1d4 + 1 different creatures, each one tethered to its body by a strand of slime that can extend up to 120 feet away. The simulacrum is an extension of the oblex, meaning that the oblex occupies its space and the simulacrum's space simultaneously. The tether is immune to damage, but it is severed if there is no opening at least 1 inch wide between the oblex and the simulacrum. The simulacrum disappears if the tether is severed."},
  ["creature.adult-oblex.mtf2014"]={title="Adult Oblex",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 218\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: ooze / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 75 (10d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 19 | CON 16 | INT 19 | WIS 12 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this distance)\n\nIdiomas: Common plus two more languages\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmorphous\n\nThe oblex can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.\n\nAversion to Fire\n\nIf the oblex takes fire damage, it has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks until the end of its next turn.\n\nSulfurous Impersonation\n\nAs a bonus action, the oblex can extrude a piece of itself that assumes the appearance of one Medium or smaller creature whose memories it has stolen. This simulacrum appears, feels, and sounds exactly like the creature it impersonates, though it smells faintly of sulfur. The oblex can impersonate 1d4 + 1 different creatures, each one tethered to its body by a strand of slime that can extend up to 120 feet away. For all practical purposes, the simulacrum is the oblex, meaning that the oblex occupies its space and the simulacrum's space simultaneously. The slimy tether is immune to damage, but it is severed if there is no opening at least 1 inch wide between the oblex's main body and the simulacrum. The simulacrum disappears if the tether is severed.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe oblex makes one pseudopod attack and uses Eat Memories.\n\nPseudopod\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 5 (2d4) psychic damage.\n\nEat Memories\n\nThe oblex targets one creature it can see within 5 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or take 18 (4d8) psychic damage and become memory drained until it finishes a short or long rest or until it benefits from the greater restoration or heal spell. Constructs, oozes, plants, and undead succeed on the save automatically.\n\nWhile memory drained, the target must roll a d4 and subtract the number rolled from any ability check or attack roll it makes. Each time the target is memory drained beyond the first, the die size increases by one: the d4 becomes a d6, the d6 becomes a d8, and so on until the die becomes a d20, at which point the target becomes unconscious for 1 hour. The effect then ends.\n\nWhen an oblex causes a target to become memory drained, the oblex learns all the languages the target knows and gains all its proficiencies, except for any saving throw proficiencies."},
  ["creature.adult-red-dracolich.tce2014"]={title="Adult Red Dracolich",subtitle="Criatura - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 137\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.adult-red-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Adult Red Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 98\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 256 (19d12 + 133)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 10 | CON 25 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h19 (2d10 + 8) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) fire damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (2d6 + 8) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h17 (2d8 + 8) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 19 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales fire in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 21 Dexterity saving throw, taking 63 (18d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 10 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 22 Dexterity saving throw or take 15 (2d6 + 8) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.adult-red-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Adult Red Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 255\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 256 (19d12 + 133)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 10 | CON 25 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 23\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB.\n\nRend\n\nm 14, reach 10 ft. h13 (1d10 + 8) Slashing damage plus 5 (2d4) Fire damage.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 21, each creature in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 59 (17d6) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCommanding Presence\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version). The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nFiery Rays\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB. The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.adult-sapphire-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Adult Sapphire Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 215\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 225 (18d12 + 108)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 14 | CON 22 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe dragon can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and can leave a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 5 (1d10) thunder damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (1d8 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nDebilitating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a pulse of high-pitched, nearly inaudible sound in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 19 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 44 (8d10) thunder damage and is incapacitated until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe dragon magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe dragon makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nTelekinetic Fling (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe dragon chooses one Small or smaller object that isn't being worn or carried that it can see within 60 feet of it, and it magically hurls the object at a creature it can see within 60 feet of the object. The target must succeed on a 17 Dexterity saving throw or take 31 (9d6) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.adult-sapphire-dragon.sads2014"]={title="Adult Sapphire Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - SADS - 2014",body="Pagina: 1\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 207 (18d12 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80, burrow: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 16 | CON 21 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 120 ft., Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe dragon can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrow speed and can choose to leave a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes two melee attacks, one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) thunder damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h19 (3d8 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nDebilitating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a pulse of high-pitched, nearly inaudible sound in a 60-foot-cone. Each creature in that cone must make a 18 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 45 (13d6) thunder damage and is incapacitated until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nTelekinetic Fling\n\nThe dragon chooses a Small or smaller object that isn't being worn or carried that it can see within 60 feet of it, and magically hurls the object at a creature it can see within 60 feet of the object. The target must succeed on a 17 Dexterity saving throw or take 15 (4d6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nTeleport (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 30 feet of it."},
  ["creature.adult-silver-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Adult Silver Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 117\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 243 (18d12 + 126)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 10 | CON 25 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h19 (2d10 + 8) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (2d6 + 8) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h17 (2d8 + 8) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 18 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Cold Breath\n\n• Paralyzing Breath\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically polymorphs into a humanoid or beast that has a challenge rating no higher than its own, or back into its true form. It reverts to its true form if it dies. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying is absorbed or borne by the new form (the dragon's choice).\n\nIn a new form, the dragon retains its alignment, hit points, Hit Dice, ability to speak, proficiencies, Legendary Resistance, lair actions, and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores, as well as this action. Its statistics and capabilities are otherwise replaced by those of the new form, except any class features or legendary actions of that form.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 10 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 22 Dexterity saving throw or take 15 (2d6 + 8) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.adult-silver-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Adult Silver Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 279\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 216 (16d12 + 112)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 10 | CON 25 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of (A) Paralyzing Breath or (B) Spellcasting to cast XPHB.\n\nRend\n\nm 13, reach 10 ft. h17 (2d8 + 8) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Cold damage.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 20, each creature in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 54 (12d8) Cold damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nParalyzing Breath\n\ncon 20, each creature in a 60-foot XPHB. 1 The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn, when it repeats the save. 2 The target has the XPHB condition, and it repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nChill\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB. The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nCold Gale\n\ndex 19, each creature in a 60-foot-long, 10-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Cold damage, and the target is pushed up to 30 feet straight away from the dragon. actSaveSuccess Half damage only. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.adult-solar-dragon.bam2014"]={title="Adult Solar Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 52\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 200 (16d12 + 96)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 90\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 15 | CON 22 | INT 15 | WIS 16 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 180 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe dragon doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nNebulous Thoughts\n\nMagical attempts to read the dragon's mind or glean its thoughts fail automatically.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe dragon deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe dragon doesn't require air.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and one Tail attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h14 (2d6 + 7) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) radiant damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h10 (1d6 + 7) bludgeoning damage.\n\nPhotonic Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a flashing mote of radiant energy that travels to a point the dragon can see within 180 feet of itself, then blossoms into a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on that point. Each creature in the sphere must make a 19 Constitution saving throw, taking 55 (10d10) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes one Tail attack.\n\nBurst of Light (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon emits magical light in a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on itself. Each creature in this area must succeed on a 23 Wisdom saving throw or be blinded until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.adult-spirit-dragon.fraif2014"]={title="Adult Spirit Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 278\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 207 (18d12 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 15 | CON 21 | INT 20 | WIS 15 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of (A) Time-Warping Breath or (B) Spellcasting to cast XPHB.\n\nRend\n\nm 11, reach 10 ft. h15 (2d8 + 6) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage.\n\nRuinous Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 18, each creature in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 63 (14d8) Necrotic damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nTime-Warping Breath\n\nwis 18, each creature that isn't currently affected by this breath in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target's XPHB is halved, it can't take Reactions, and it can take either an action or a XPHB on its turn, not both. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack.\n\nShattering Wave\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB.\n\nUnearth Ruins\n\nThe dragon magically raises broken, ancient ruins in a 20-foot-radius, 60-foot-high XPHB centered on a point it can see within 120 feet. Ground in the XPHB becomes XPHB. Each creature in the XPHB when it appears is subjected to the following effect. str 18. actSaveFail 5 (2d4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the XPHB condition. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn."},
  ["creature.adult-time-dragon.mpp2014"]={title="Adult Time Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 18\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 250 (20d12 + 120)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 14 | CON 23 | INT 23 | WIS 16 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h14 (2d6 + 7) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) force damage.\n\nTime Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a wave of shimmering light in a 60-foot cone. Nonmagical objects and vegetation in that area that aren't being worn or carried crumble to dust. Each creature in that area must make a 20 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 36 (8d8) force damage and is magically weakened as it is desynchronized from the time stream. While the creature is in this state, attack rolls against it have advantage, and it has the poisoned condition. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only. A weakened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself after it succeeds on three of these saves.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nReactive Rend\n\nAfter using Legendary Resistance or in response to being hit by an attack roll, the dragon makes one Rend attack.\n\nSlow Time\n\nImmediately after a creature the dragon can see ends its turn, the dragon targets a creature it can see within 60 feet of itself that is weakened by its Time Breath. Until the weakened effect ends on the target, its speed becomes 0, and its speed can't increase.\n\nTime Slip\n\nThe dragon halves the damage it takes from an attack made against it, provided it can see the attacker. The dragon can then immediately teleport, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["creature.adult-topaz-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Adult Topaz Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 210 (20d12 + 80)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 12 | CON 19 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe both air and water.\n\nFabricate (1/Day)\n\nThe dragon can cast fabricate, requiring no spell components and using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) necrotic damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nDesiccating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales yellowish necrotic energy in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 17 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 35 (10d6) necrotic damage and is weakened until the end of its next turn. A weakened creature has disadvantage on Strength-based ability checks and Strength saving throws, and the creature's weapon attacks that rely on Strength deal half damage. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't weakened.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe dragon magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe dragon makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nEssential Reduction (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe dragon targets a creature or an object not being worn or carried that it can see within 60 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 17 Constitution saving throw or take 28 (8d6) necrotic damage. If this damage reduces the target to 0 hit points, it crumbles to dust."},
  ["creature.adult-white-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Adult White Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 101\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 200 (16d12 + 96)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 10 | CON 22 | INT 8 | WIS 12 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIce Walk\n\nThe dragon can move across and climb icy surfaces without needing to make an ability check. Additionally, difficult terrain composed of ice or snow doesn't cost it extra movement.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) cold damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h15 (2d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 14 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales an icy blast in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 19 Constitution saving throw, taking 54 (12d8) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 10 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 19 Dexterity saving throw or take 13 (2d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.adult-white-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Adult White Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 329\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / H\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 200 (16d12 + 96)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 10 | CON 22 | INT 8 | WIS 12 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIce Walk\n\nThe dragon can move across and climb icy surfaces without needing to make an ability check. Additionally, XPHB composed of ice or snow doesn't cost it extra movement.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nFrightful Presence\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 11, reach 10 ft. h13 (2d6 + 6) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Cold damage.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 19, each creature in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 54 (12d8) Cold damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nFreezing Burst\n\ncon 14, each creature in a 30-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point the dragon can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 7 (2d6) Cold damage, and the target's XPHB is 0 until the end of the target's next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["feature.advanced-artifice.efa2014.artificer.base.14"]={title="Advanced Artifice",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 11\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nMagic Item Savant\n\nYou can now attune to up to five magic items at once.\n\nRefreshed Genius\n\nWhen you finish a XPHB, you regain one expended use of your Artificer feature."},
  ["creature.advanced-detention-drone.bmt2014"]={title="Advanced Detention Drone",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30"},
  ["feature.adventurer-s-atlas.efa2014.artificer.cartographer.3"]={title="Adventurer's Atlas",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB while holding XPHB, you can use that tool to create a set of magical maps by touching at least two creatures (one of whom can be yourself), up to a maximum number of creatures equal to 1 plus your Intelligence modifier (minimum of two creatures). Each target receives a magical map, which constantly updates to show the relative position of all the map holders but is illegible to all others. The maps last until you die or until you use this feature again, at which point any existing maps created by this feature immediately vanish.\n\nWhile carrying the map, a target gains the following benefits.\n\nAwareness\n\nThe target adds 1d4 to its XPHB rolls.\n\nPositioning\n\nThe target knows the location of all other map holders that are on the same plane of existence as itself. When casting a spell or creating another effect that requires being able to see the effect's target, a map holder can target another map holder regardless of sight or cover, so long as the other map holder is still within the effect's range."},
  ["magicitem.adventurer-s-ring.frhof2014"]={title="Adventurer's Ring",subtitle="Item Magico - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 132\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nWhile the cover on this ring is open, the ring produces a flame that creates no heat and consumes no fuel. It sheds XPHB in a 20-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 20 feet. As a XPHB, you can close the cover, smothering the flame, or open it again."},
  ["magicitem.adze-of-annam.bgg2014"]={title="Adze of Annam",subtitle="Item Magico - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 110\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nThis massive adze is said to have been wielded by All-Father Annam, not as a weapon but as the tool he used to shape the various worlds of the Material Plane eons ago.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nThe adze has the following random properties, determined by rolling on the appropriate table in the Dungeon Master's Guide:\n\n• 2 dmg properties\n\n• 1 dmg property\n\n• 2 dmg properties\n\nMagic Weapon\n\nWhen a creature attunes to the adze, the artifact magically adjusts its size so that creature can wield it as a greataxe. The adze is a magic weapon that grants a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. On a hit, the adze deals an additional 3d12 force damage. It also deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\nDivine Mattock\n\nAs an action, you can call upon the might of the All-Father and use the adze to cast move earth or fabricate. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["deity.aegir.phb2014"]={title="Aegir",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 299"},
  ["creature.aegisaur.psx2014"]={title="Aegisaur",subtitle="Criatura - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.aeorian-absorber.egw2014"]={title="Aeorian Absorber",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 283\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 171 (18d10 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 18 | CON 18 | INT 6 | WIS 14 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Draconic but can't speak\n\nImunidades: necrotic, radiant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe absorber has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nPounce\n\nIf the absorber moves at least 20 feet straight toward a creature and then hits its claws attack on the same turn, that target must succeed on a 17 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone. If the target is prone, the absorber can make one bite attack against it as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe absorber makes three attacks: one with its bite or Mind Bolt and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h10 (1d10 + 5) piercing damage plus 5 (1d10) force damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d6 + 5) slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) force damage.\n\nMind Bolt\n\nrs 8 to hit, range 120 ft., one creature. h22 (4d10) psychic damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nTail Ray\n\nWhen the absorber takes damage from a spell, the absorber takes only half the triggering damage. If the spellcaster is within 60 feet of the absorber, the absorber can force the caster to make a 16 Dexterity saving throw. Unless the save succeeds, the caster takes the other half of the damage."},
  ["creature.aeorian-nullifier.egw2014"]={title="Aeorian Nullifier",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 283\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 180 (19d10 + 76)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 7 | WIS 14 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Draconic but can't speak\n\nImunidades: necrotic, radiant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHorrid Gnashing\n\nThe nullifier's mouths gnash incoherently while it can see any enemies. Each creature that starts its turn within 20 feet of the nullifier and can hear it must make a 16 Wisdom saving throw. Unless the save succeeds, the creature rolls a d8 to determine what it does during the current turn:\n\n• 1-4:\n\n• 5-6:\n\n• 7-8:\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe nullifier has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe nullifier makes three attacks: one with its bites and two with its claws.\n\nBites\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h17 (2d12 + 4) piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) force damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 11 (2d10) force damage, and the target is grappled (escape 16) if it's a creature. The nullifier has two claws, each of which can grapple one creature.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nCounterspell\n\nThe nullifier attempts to interrupt a creature that it can see within 60 feet in the process of casting a spell. If the creature is casting a spell of 3rd level or lower, its spell fails and has no effect. If it is casting a spell of 4th level or higher, the nullifier makes a Charisma check with a DC equal to 10 + the spell's level. On a success, the creature's spell fails and has no effect."},
  ["creature.aeorian-reverser.egw2014"]={title="Aeorian Reverser",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 284\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 133 (14d10 + 56)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 16 | CON 18 | INT 6 | WIS 14 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Draconic but can't speak\n\nImunidades: necrotic, radiant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe reverser has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe reverser makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, range 5 ft., one creature. h11 (1d12 + 5) piercing damage plus 6 (1d12) force damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d6 + 5) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) force damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nReversal\n\nWhen a creature the reverser can see within 30 feet of it regains hit points, the reverser reduces the number of hit points regained to 0, and the reverser deals 13 (3d8) force damage to the creature."},
  ["deity.aerdrie-faenya.mtf2014"]={title="Aerdrie Faenya",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43"},
  ["deity.aerdrie-faenya.scag2014"]={title="Aerdrie Faenya",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 23"},
  ["item.aerenal-trinket.erlw2014"]={title="Aerenal Trinket",subtitle="Item - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nd8 | Trinket\n\n1 | A bronzewood ring inscribed with the Elvish word for \"hope\"\n\n2 | A dried flower; if it's placed in water, it blooms\n\n3 | An ebony locket; when it's opened, an elven voice whispers \"Always\"\n\n4 | A tiny skull carved from dark wood\n\n5 | A finger bone inscribed with an unknown sigil\n\n6 | An ivory flute which produces no sound\n\n7 | A small journal made from preserved leaves\n\n8 | A book of poetry written by undead elves"},
  ["creature.aerisi-kalinoth.pota2014"]={title="Aerisi Kalinoth",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 13/16\n\nPV: 66 (12d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 17 | WIS 10 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Auran, Common, Elvish\n\nResistencias: lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nAerisi has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put her to sleep.\n\nHowling Defeat\n\nWhen Aerisi drops to 0 hit points, her body disappears in a howling whirlwind that disperses quickly and harmlessly. Anything she is wearing or carrying is left behind.\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf Aerisi fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nWindvane\n\nmw,rw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h9 (1d6 + 6) piercing damage, or 10 (1d8 + 6) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack, plus 3 (1d6) lightning damage."},
  ["creature.aerosaur.bgg2014"]={title="Aerosaur",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 128\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / G\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 155 (10d20 + 50)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 120\n\nSTR 26 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 3 | WIS 10 | CHA 5\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe aerosaur has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe aerosaur makes one Bite attack and one Talons attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h27 (3d12 + 8) piercing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it has the grappled condition (escape 18). Until this grapple ends, the target has the restrained condition, and the aerosaur can't Bite another target.\n\nTalons\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h24 (3d10 + 8) slashing damage.\n\nWing Gusts {@recharge 5}\n\nThe aerosaur beats its wings, creating bursts of thunderous force. Each creature within 10 feet of the aerosaur must make a 20 Strength saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 38 (7d10) thunder damage, is pushed up to 30 feet horizontally from the aerosaur, and has the prone condition. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage and is pushed up to 15 feet horizontally from the aerosaur."},
  ["creature.aerosaur-large.psx2014"]={title="Aerosaur (Large)",subtitle="Criatura - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.aerosaur-small.psx2014"]={title="Aerosaur (Small)",subtitle="Criatura - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.aeshma.coa2014"]={title="Aeshma",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 261\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 45 (7d8 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 16 | CON 14 | INT 14 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAeshma makes two attacks using his Shortsword, Hand Crossbow, or a combination of the two.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nHand Crossbow\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nCunning\n\nAeshma takes the Dash, Disengage, or Hide action."},
  ["species.aetherborn.psk2014"]={title="Aetherborn",subtitle="Especie - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 17\n\nAge\n\nAetherborn come into being as adults and live no more than a few years.\n\nAlignment\n\nAs a rule, aetherborn are driven by hedonism and self-interest, making them neutral at best and thoroughly evil at worst. Neutral aetherborn might devote much of their time (and wealth) to parties and social activity, while evil aetherborn are usually involved in the criminal underworld.\n\nSize\n\nAetherborn are about the same size as humans, ranging from 5 to 6 feet tall. They are quite light—only about 100 pounds—and their weight diminishes as they age and more and more of their substance returns to the aethersphere. Your size is Medium.\n\nDarkvision\n\nThanks to your heritage, you have superior vision in dark and dim conditions. You can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nBorn of Aether\n\nYou have resistance to necrotic damage.\n\nMenacing\n\nYou have proficiency in the Intimidation skill.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and two other languages of your choice.\n\nGift of the Aetherborn\n\nAn unknown aetherborn, desperately seeking a means to extend their short life, discovered a process of transformation that prolonged their existence—by giving them the ability to feed on the life essence of other beings. Since then, other aetherborn have learned and carried out this monstrous transformation, and aetherborn with this \"gift\" have become a small minority among an already small population.\n\nA gifted aetherborn has the ability to drain the life essence of other beings. Similar to the way heat is transferred from a warm object to a cold one, a gifted aetherborn need only touch another living being with a clawed hand to draw life essence out, fueling their own continued existence while draining strength and vitality from their victim.\n\nFor many aetherborn, living as they do for indulgence and instant gratification, the concepts of \"want\" and \"need\" are virtually synonymous. But Aetherborn with this gift understand what it is to truly need, for they develop a hunger for life essence that far exceeds any desires they might have felt before their transformation. A gifted aetherborn who abstains from this feeding deteriorates even more rapidly than other aetherborn, while enduring unspeakable agony caused by the deprivation of life energy.\n\nAt the DM's option, an aetherborn character can research methods of achieving this dark \"gift.\" The process is similar to inventing and manufacturing a rare magic item (see \"PS-K\" earlier in this document). But rather than aether, the process requires a variety of rare unguents and unusual ingredients that make up the cost of researching and undergoing the transformation.\n\nAn aetherborn with this gift gains the Drain Life ability: a natural attack that deals 1d6 necrotic damage and restores the same number of hit points to the aetherborn. However, if the aetherborn goes for 7 days without dealing this damage, their hit point maximum is reduced by 1d6 per week. This reduction can't be removed until the aetherborn has used their Drain Life ability and completed a long rest."},
  ["creature.affliction-devil-kocrachon.coa2014"]={title="Affliction Devil (Kocrachon)",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 236\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 104 (16d8 + 32)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 19 | CON 15 | INT 17 | WIS 12 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: cold, fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the kocrachon's darkvision.\n\nInfernal Rot\n\nA creature afflicted with this disease has the poisoned condition until the disease ends. While diseased, creatures gain no benefits from a long rest, gaining exhaustion when necessary. If a creature dies while afflicted with Infernal Rot, its corpse transforms into a newborn kocrachon after 4 (1d8) days.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe kocrachon has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSadism\n\nThe kocrachon gains a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls for each different creature it damaged on its previous turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe kocrachon makes three Claw attacks. It can replace one of the attacks with a Proboscis attack.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nProboscis\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h10 (1d12 + 4) piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) poison damage. Creatures damaged by this attack must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or suffer the Infernal Rot disease."},
  ["creature.afsoun-ghorbani.jttrc2014"]={title="Afsoun Ghorbani",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 162\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["spell.aganazzar-s-scorcher.xge2024"]={title="Aganazzar's Scorcher",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 150\n\nA line of roaring flame 30 feet long and 5 feet wide emanates from you in a direction you choose. Each creature in the line must make a Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 3d8 fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.agathe-silverspoon.crcotn2014"]={title="Agathe Silverspoon",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.agdon-longscarf.wbtw2014"]={title="Agdon Longscarf",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 73\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 36 (8d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 35\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 20 | CON 11 | INT 11 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEvasion\n\nIf Agdon is subjected to an effect that allows him to make a Dexterity saving throw to take only half damage, he instead takes no damage if he succeeds on the saving throw and only half damage if he fails, provided he isn't incapacitated.\n\nStanding Leap\n\nAgdon's long jump is up to 20 feet and his high jump is up to 10 feet, with or without a running start.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAgdon makes two Branding Iron or Dagger attacks.\n\nBranding Iron\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (3d6) fire damage, and the target is magically branded. Agdon is invisible to creatures branded in this way. The brand disappears after 24 hours, or it can be removed from a creature or object by any spell that ends a curse.\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h7 (1d4 + 5) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nQuick Fingers\n\nAgdon targets one creature within 5 feet of him that he can see and makes a Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check, with a DC equal to 1 + the target's passive Wisdom (Perception) score. On a successful check, Agdon pilfers one object weighing 1 pound or less that the target has in its possession but not in its grasp, without the target noticing the theft.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUncanny Dodge\n\nAgdon halves the damage that he takes from an attack that hits him. He must be able to see the attacker."},
  ["feat.agent-of-order.sato2014"]={title="Agent of Order",subtitle="Feat - SatO - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nYou can channel cosmic forces of order to gain these benefits:\n\n• Stasis Strike Once per turn, when you damage a creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself, you can deal an extra 1d8 force damage to the target, and it must make a Wisdom saving throw (DC equal to 8 + your proficiency bonus + the modifier of the spellcasting ability you chose for the Scion of the Outer Planes feat) as spectral bindings try to ensnare it. On a successful save, the target escapes. On a failed save, the target has the restrained condition until the start of your next turn. These bindings manifest as chains or some other symbol of stasis. You can use this benefit a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},
  ["background.agent-of-the-ninth-quill.au2014"]={title="Agent of the Ninth Quill",subtitle="Background - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["feature.agile-parry.xge2024.monk.kensei.3"]={title="Agile Parry",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 34\n\nIf you make an unarmed strike as part of the Attack action on your turn and are holding a kensei weapon, you can use it to defend yourself if it is a melee weapon. You gain a +2 bonus to AC until the start of your next turn, while the weapon is in your hand and you aren't incapacitated."},
  ["feature.agile-strikes.xphb2024.bard.dance.3"]={title="Agile Strikes",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 64\n\nWhen you expend a use of your Bardic Inspiration as part of an action, a XPHB, or a XPHB, you can make one XPHB as part of that action, XPHB, or XPHB."},
  ["language.aglarondan.frhof2014"]={title="Aglarondan",subtitle="Idioma - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 49"},
  ["optionalfeature.agonizing-blast.phb2014"]={title="Agonizing Blast",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 110\n\nWhen you cast eldritch blast, add your Charisma modifier to the damage it deals on a hit."},
  ["optionalfeature.agonizing-blast.xphb2024"]={title="Agonizing Blast",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 155\n\nChoose one of your known spells that deals damage. You can add your Charisma modifier to that spell's damage rolls.\n\nRepeatable\n\nYou can gain this invocation more than once. Each time you do so, choose a different eligible cantrip."},
  ["creature.agony.lox2014"]={title="Agony",subtitle="Criatura - LoX - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.ahmaergo.wdh2014"]={title="Ahmaergo",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 193\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 143 (22d8 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 15 | CON 14 | INT 15 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish, Undercommon\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDwarven Resilience\n\nAhmaergo has advantage on saving throws against being poisoned.\n\nIndomitable (2/Day)\n\nAhmaergo can reroll a saving throw that he fails. He must use the new roll.\n\nSecond Wind (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nAs a bonus action, Ahmaergo can regain 20 hit points.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAhmaergo makes three attacks with his greataxe.\n\nGreataxe\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (1d12 + 5) slashing damage, plus 7 (2d6) slashing damage if Ahmaergo has more than half his hit points remaining.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["spell.aid.phb2014"]={title="Aid",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\nYour spell bolsters your allies with toughness and resolve. Choose up to three creatures within range. Each target's hit point maximum and current hit points increase by 5 for the duration."},
  ["spell.aid.xphb2024"]={title="Aid",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 239\n\nChoose up to three creatures within range. Each target's XPHB maximum and current XPHB increase by 5 for the duration."},
  ["spell.air-bubble.aag2014"]={title="Air Bubble",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - AAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 22\n\nYou create a spectral globe around the head of a willing creature you can see within range. The globe is filled with fresh air that lasts until the spell ends. If the creature has more than one head, the globe of air appears around only one of its heads (which is all the creature needs to avoid suffocation, assuming that all its heads share the same respiratory system)."},
  ["creature.air-elemental.mm2014"]={title="Air Elemental",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 124\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 90 (12d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: fly: 90\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 20 | CON 14 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Auran\n\nResistencias: lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAir Form\n\nThe elemental can enter a hostile creature's space and stop there. It can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe elemental makes two slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage.\n\nWhirlwind {@recharge 4}\n\nEach creature in the elemental's space must make a 13 Strength saving throw. On a failure, a target takes 15 (3d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage and is flung up 20 feet away from the elemental in a random direction and knocked prone. If a thrown target strikes an object, such as a wall or floor, the target takes 3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage for every 10 feet it was thrown. If the target is thrown at another creature, that creature must succeed on a 13 Dexterity saving throw or take the same damage and be knocked prone.\n\nIf the saving throw is successful, the target takes half the bludgeoning damage and isn't flung away or knocked prone."},
  ["creature.air-elemental.xmm2024"]={title="Air Elemental",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 13\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 90 (12d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 90\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 20 | CON 14 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Primordial (Auran)\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, lightning, piercing, slashing\n\nImunidades: poison, thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAir Form\n\nThe elemental can enter a creature's space and stop there. It can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch without expending extra movement to do so.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe elemental makes two Thunderous Slam attacks.\n\nThunderous Slam\n\nm 8, reach 10 ft. h14 (2d8 + 5) Thunder damage.\n\nWhirlwind {@recharge 4}\n\nstr 13, one Medium or smaller creature in the elemental's space. actSaveFail 24 (4d10 + 2) Thunder damage, and the target is pushed up to 20 feet straight away from the elemental and has the XPHB condition. actSaveSuccess Half damage only."},
  ["creature.air-elemental-myrmidon.mpmm2014"]={title="Air Elemental Myrmidon",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 117 (18d8 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 9 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Auran, one language of its creator's choice\n\nResistencias: lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe myrmidon makes three Flail attacks.\n\nFlail\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) force damage.\n\nLightning Strike {@recharge}\n\nThe myrmidon makes one Flail attack. On a hit, the target takes an extra 18 (4d8) lightning damage, and the target must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or be stunned until the end of the myrmidon's next turn."},
  ["creature.air-elemental-myrmidon.mtf2014"]={title="Air Elemental Myrmidon",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 202\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 117 (18d8 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 9 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Auran, one language of its creator's choice\n\nResistencias: lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe myrmidon's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe myrmidon makes three flail attacks.\n\nFlail\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage.\n\nLightning Strike {@recharge}\n\nThe myrmidon makes one flail attack. On a hit, the target takes an extra 18 (4d8) lightning damage, and the target must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or be stunned until the end of the myrmidon's next turn."},
  ["creature.air-totem-elemental.psx2014"]={title="Air Totem Elemental",subtitle="Criatura - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.airship.dmg2014"]={title="Airship",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.airship.xphb2024"]={title="Airship",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 230\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["deity.akadi.scag2014"]={title="Akadi",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 21"},
  ["magicitem.akmon-hammer-of-purphoros.mot2014"]={title="Akmon, Hammer of Purphoros",subtitle="Item Magico - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 198\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nPurphoros's hammer works wonders and disasters, the god of the forge using it to craft ground-breaking marvels and dangerous inventions in equal measure. Purphoros rarely bestows Akmon on mortals but occasionally leaves it unattended at his forge in Mount Velus. When Purphoros does permit a mortal to use the hammer, it's usually so they might bring an important work into being, wreck a force of destruction, or forge something remarkable somewhere the god isn't welcome.\n\nHammer of the Forge\n\nThis magic warhammer grants a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. When you hit with an attack using it, the target takes an extra 3d10 fire damage.\n\nBlessing of the Forge\n\nIf you are a worshiper of Purphoros, you gain all the following benefits for which you have the required piety:\n\n• Piety 10+\n\n• Piety 25+\n\n• Piety 50+\n\nIf you aren't a worshiper of Purphoros, the hammer has 2 randomly determined dmg properties.\n\nSee \"Artifacts\" in chapter 7 of the Dungeon Master's Guide for details on randomly determined properties.\n\nReforged\n\nWhile holding the hammer, you have resistance to fire damage and are immune to exhaustion. Additionally, you have proficiency with PHB and have advantage on all ability checks made using them.\n\nSpells\n\nWhile the hammer is on your person, you can use an action to cast one of the following spells (save 18): animate objects, heat metal, fabricate, magic weapon, mending, shatter. Once you use the hammer to cast a spell, the spell can't be cast again from it until the next dusk.\n\nDestroying the Hammer\n\nTo destroy the hammer, it must be taken to the realm of Tizerus, in the Underworld. There it must be coated in clay from the Mire of Punishment. The heat of the hammer hardens the clay, which fuses to it after one month. Once fully hardened, the clay-covered hammer must be swallowed and digested by a kraken."},
  ["creature.akroan-hoplite.mot2014"]={title="Akroan Hoplite",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 52 (8d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 16 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 14 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHold the Line\n\nWhile the hoplite is holding a spear, other creatures provoke an opportunity attack from the hoplite when they move within 5 feet of it. When the hoplite hits a creature with an opportunity attack using its spear, the creature takes an extra 4 (1d8) piercing damage, and the creature's speed becomes 0 for the rest of the turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe hoplite makes three melee attacks or two ranged attacks.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., or range 20/60 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage, or 7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nShield Bash\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h5 (1d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."},
  ["creature.al-chaia.wdmm2014"]={title="Al'chaia",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 218\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nPV: 140 (14d8 + 28)"},
  ["creature.alagarthas.wbtw2014"]={title="Alagarthas",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 52 (8d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 11 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBrave\n\nAlagarthas has advantage on saving throws against being frightened.\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nAlagarthas has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put him to sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAlagarthas makes two melee attacks.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 bludgeoning damage.\n\nLeadership (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nFor 1 minute, Alagarthas can utter a special command or warning whenever a nonhostile creature that it can see within 30 feet of it makes an attack roll or a saving throw. The creature can add a d4 to its roll provided it can hear and understand him. A creature can benefit from only one Leadership die at a time. This effect ends if Alagarthas is incapacitated."},
  ["charoption.alagondar-scion.idrotf2014"]={title="Alagondar Scion",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 264\n\nI'm a scion of the Alagondar bloodline and the only known heir to the crown of Neverwinter. If Dagult Neverember, the city's lord-regent, learns that I'm alive, he'll send assassins to kill me."},
  ["spell.alarm.phb2014"]={title="Alarm",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\nYou set an alarm against unwanted intrusion. Choose a door, a window, or an area within range that is no larger than a 20-foot cube. Until the spell ends, an alarm alerts you whenever a Tiny or larger creature touches or enters the warded area. When you cast the spell, you can designate creatures that won't set off the alarm. You also choose whether the alarm is mental or audible.\n\nA mental alarm alerts you with a ping in your mind if you are within 1 mile of the warded area. This ping awakens you if you are sleeping.\n\nAn audible alarm produces the sound of a hand bell for 10 seconds within 60 feet."},
  ["spell.alarm.xphb2024"]={title="Alarm",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 239\n\nYou set an alarm against intrusion. Choose a door, a window, or an area within range that is no larger than a 20-foot XPHB. Until the spell ends, an alarm alerts you whenever a creature touches or enters the warded area. When you cast the spell, you can designate creatures that won't set off the alarm. You also choose whether the alarm is audible or mental:\n\n• Audible Alarm The alarm produces the sound of a handbell for 10 seconds within 60 feet of the warded area.\n\n• Mental Alarm You are alerted by a mental ping if you are within 1 mile of the warded area. This ping awakens you if you're asleep."},
  ["creature.alastrah.skt2014"]={title="Alastrah",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant\n\nSTR 14\n\nIdiomas: Giant\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClub\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["deity.alathrien-druanna.mtf2014"]={title="Alathrien Druanna",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43"},
  ["creature.alax-jadescales.lrdt2014"]={title="Alax Jadescales",subtitle="Criatura - LRDT - 2014",body="Pagina: 11\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 58 (9d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 10 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 16 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAlax makes two Fire Strike attacks.\n\nFire Strike\n\nms,rs 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) fire damage.\n\nBreath Weapon (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nAlax exhales a 15-foot cone of fire. Each creature in that area must make a 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 14 (4d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.albino-dwarf-spirit-warrior.toa2014"]={title="Albino Dwarf Spirit Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 30 (4d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 13 | CON 17 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDwarven Resilience\n\nThe dwarf has advantage on saving throws against poison.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHandaxe\n\nmw,rw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d6 + 1) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.albino-dwarf-warrior.toa2014"]={title="Albino Dwarf Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 30 (4d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 13 | CON 17 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDwarven Resilience\n\nThe dwarf has advantage on saving throws against poison.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHandaxe\n\nmw,rw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d6 + 1) slashing damage."},
  ["magicitem.alchemical-compendium.tce2014"]={title="Alchemical Compendium",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nAcrid odors cling to this stained, heavy volume. The book's metal fittings are copper, iron, lead, silver, and gold, some frozen mid-transition from one metal to another. When found, the book contains the following spells: enlarge/reduce, feather fall, flesh to stone, gaseous form, magic weapon, and polymorph. It functions as a spellbook for you.\n\nWhile you are holding the book, you can use it as a spellcasting focus for your wizard spells.\n\nThe book has 3 charges, and it regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. You can use the charges in the following ways while holding it:\n\n• If you spend 1 minute studying the book, you can expend 1 charge to replace one of your prepared wizard spells with a different spell in the book. The new spell must be of the transmutation school.\n\n• As an action, you can touch a nonmagical object that isn't being worn or carried and spend a number of charges to transform the target into another object. For 1 charge, the object can be no larger than 1 foot on a side. You can spend additional charges to increase the maximum dimensions by 2 feet per charge. The new object must have a gold value equal to or less than the original."},
  ["feature.alchemical-savant.efa2014.artificer.alchemist.5"]={title="Alchemical Savant",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 14\n\nWhenever you cast a spell using your XPHB as the XPHB, you gain a bonus to one roll of the spell. That roll must restore XPHB or be a damage roll that deals Acid, Fire, or Poison damage. The bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum bonus of +1)."},
  ["feature.alchemical-savant.tce2014.artificer.alchemist.5"]={title="Alchemical Savant",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 14\n\nAt 5th level, you develop masterful command of magical chemicals, enhancing the healing and damage you create through them. Whenever you cast a spell using your PHB as the spellcasting focus, you gain a bonus to one roll of the spell. That roll must restore hit points or be a damage roll that deals acid, fire, necrotic, or poison damage, and the bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1)."},
  ["subclass.alchemist.efa2014.artificer.alchemist.0"]={title="Alchemist",subtitle="Subclasse - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist\n\nPagina: 12\n\nCraft Magic Elixirs and Potions\n\nAn Alchemist is an expert at combining reagents to produce magical effects. Alchemists use their creations to give life and to leech it away.\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist\n\nPagina: 14\n\nAn Alchemist is an expert at combining reagents to produce mystical effects. Alchemists use their creations to give life and to leech it away. Alchemy is the oldest of artificer traditions, and its versatility has long been valued during times of war and peace.\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist Spells\n\nPagina: 13\n\nWhen you reach an Artificer level specified in the Alchemist Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nArtificer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist Spells\n\nPagina: 14\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Alchemist Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.\n\nArtificer Level | Spell\n\n3rd | healing word, ray of sickness\n\n5th | flaming sphere, Melf's acid arrow\n\n9th | gaseous form, mass healing word\n\n13th | blight, death ward\n\n17th | cloudkill, raise dead\n\nNivel 3 - Experimental Elixir\n\nPagina: 13\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB while holding XPHB, you can use that tool to magically produce two elixirs. For each elixir, roll on the Experimental Elixir table for the elixir's effect, which is triggered when someone drinks the elixir. The elixir appears in a vial, and the vial vanishes when the elixir is drunk or poured out. If any elixir remains when you finish a XPHB, the elixir and its vial vanish.\n\nDrinking an Elixir\n\nAs a XPHB, a creature can drink the elixir or administer it to another creature within 5 feet of itself.\n\nCreating Additional Elixirs\n\nAs a XPHB action while holding XPHB, you can expend one spell slot to create another elixir. When you do so, you choose its effect from the Experimental Elixir table rather than rolling.\n\nWhen you reach certain Artificer levels, you can make an additional elixir at the end of each XPHB: a total of three at level 5, four at level 9, and five at level 15.\n\n1d6 | Effect\n\n1 | Healing. The drinker regains a number of XPHB equal to 2d8 plus your Intelligence modifier. The number of XPHB restored increases by 1d8 when you reach Artificer levels 9 (3d8) and 15 (4d8).\n\n2 | Swiftness. The drinker's XPHB increases by 10 feet for 1 hour. This bonus increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (15 feet) and 15 (20 feet).\n\n3 | Resilience. The drinker gains a +1 bonus to AC for 10 minutes. The duration increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (1 hour) and 15 (8 hours).\n\n4 | Boldness. The drinker can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to every attack roll and saving throw they make for the next minute. The duration increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (10 minutes) and 15 (1 hour).\n\n5 | Flight. The drinker gains a XPHB of 10 feet for 10 minutes. The XPHB increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (20 feet) and 15 (30 feet).\n\n6 | You determine the elixir's effect by choosing one of the other rows in this table.\n\nNivel 3 - Experimental Elixir\n\nPagina: 14\n\nBeginning at 3rd level, whenever you finish a long rest, you can magically produce an experimental elixir in an empty flask you touch. Roll on the Experimental Elixir table for the elixir's effect, which is triggered when someone drinks the elixir. As an action, a creature can drink the elixir or administer it to an incapacitated creature.\n\nCreating an experimental elixir requires you to have PHB on your person, and any elixir you create with this feature lasts until it is drunk or until the end of your next long rest.\n\nWhen you reach certain levels in this class, you can make more elixirs at the end of a long rest: two at 6th level and three at 15th level. Roll for each elixir's effect separately. Each elixir requires its own flask.\n\nYou can create additional experimental elixirs by expending a spell slot of 1st level or higher for each one. When you do so, you use your action to create the elixir in an empty flask you touch, and you choose the elixir's effect from the Experimental Elixir table.\n\nd6 | Effect\n\n1 | Healing. The drinker regains a number of hit points equal to 2d4 + your Intelligence modifier.\n\n2 | Swiftness. The drinker's walking speed increases by 10 feet for 1 hour.\n\n3 | Resilience. The drinker gains a +1 bonus to AC for 10 minutes.\n\n4 | Boldness. The drinker can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to every attack roll and saving throw they make for the next minute.\n\n5 | Flight. The drinker gains a flying speed of 10 feet for 10 minutes.\n\n6 | Transformation. The drinker's body is transformed as if by the alter self spell. The drinker determines the transformation caused by the spell, the effects of which last for 10 minutes.\n\nNivel 3 - Tool Proficiency\n\nPagina: 14\n\nWhen you adopt this specialization at 3rd level, you gain proficiency with PHB. If you already have this proficiency, you gain proficiency with one other type of PHB of your choice.\n\nNivel 3 - Tool Proficiency\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nPagina: 12\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nTool Proficiency\n\nYou gain proficiency with XPHB and the XPHB. If you already have one of these proficiencies, you gain proficiency with one other type of XPHB of your choice (or with two other types if you have both).\n\nPotion Crafting\n\nWhen you brew a potion using the crafting rules in the XDMG, the amount of time required to craft it is halved.\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nNivel 5 - Alchemical Savant\n\nPagina: 14\n\nWhenever you cast a spell using your XPHB as the XPHB, you gain a bonus to one roll of the spell. That roll must restore XPHB or be a damage roll that deals Acid, Fire, or Poison damage. The bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum bonus of +1).\n\nNivel 5 - Alchemical Savant\n\nPagina: 14\n\nAt 5th level, you develop masterful command of magical chemicals, enhancing the healing and damage you create through them. Whenever you cast a spell using your PHB as the spellcasting focus, you gain a bonus to one roll of the spell. That roll must restore hit points or be a damage roll that deals acid, fire, necrotic, or poison damage, and the bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).\n\nNivel 9 - Restorative Reagents\n\nPagina: 14\n\nYou can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot and without preparing the spell, provided you use XPHB as the XPHB. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 9 - Restorative Reagents\n\nPagina: 14\n\nStarting at 9th level, you can incorporate restorative reagents into some of your works:\n\n• Whenever a creature drinks an experimental elixir you created, the creature gains temporary hit points equal to 2d6 + your Intelligence modifier (minimum of 1 temporary hit point).\n\n• You can cast lesser restoration without expending a spell slot and without preparing the spell, provided you use PHB as the spellcasting focus. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery\n\nPagina: 14\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nAlchemical Eruption\n\nWhen you cast an Artificer spell that deals Acid, Fire, or Poison damage to a target, you can also deal 2d8 Force damage to that target. You can use this benefit only once on each of your turns.\n\nChemical Resistance\n\nYou gain XPHB to Acid damage and Poison damage. You also gain XPHB to the XPHB condition.\n\nConjured Cauldron\n\nYou can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot, without preparing the spell, and without Material components, provided you use XPHB as the XPHB. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery\n\nPagina: 14\n\nBy 15th level, you have been exposed to so many chemicals that they pose little risk to you, and you can use them to quickly end certain ailments:\n\n• You gain resistance to acid damage and poison damage, and you are immune to the poisoned condition.\n\n• You can cast greater restoration and heal without expending a spell slot, without preparing the spell, and without material components, provided you use PHB as the spellcasting focus. Once you cast either spell with this feature, you can't cast that spell with it again until you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery"},
  ["feature.alchemist.efa2014.artificer.alchemist.3"]={title="Alchemist",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\nCraft Magic Elixirs and Potions\n\nAn Alchemist is an expert at combining reagents to produce magical effects. Alchemists use their creations to give life and to leech it away."},
  ["subclass.alchemist.tce2014.artificer.alchemist.0"]={title="Alchemist",subtitle="Subclasse - TCE - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist\n\nPagina: 12\n\nCraft Magic Elixirs and Potions\n\nAn Alchemist is an expert at combining reagents to produce magical effects. Alchemists use their creations to give life and to leech it away.\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist\n\nPagina: 14\n\nAn Alchemist is an expert at combining reagents to produce mystical effects. Alchemists use their creations to give life and to leech it away. Alchemy is the oldest of artificer traditions, and its versatility has long been valued during times of war and peace.\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist Spells\n\nPagina: 13\n\nWhen you reach an Artificer level specified in the Alchemist Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nArtificer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist Spells\n\nPagina: 14\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Alchemist Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.\n\nArtificer Level | Spell\n\n3rd | healing word, ray of sickness\n\n5th | flaming sphere, Melf's acid arrow\n\n9th | gaseous form, mass healing word\n\n13th | blight, death ward\n\n17th | cloudkill, raise dead\n\nNivel 3 - Experimental Elixir\n\nPagina: 13\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB while holding XPHB, you can use that tool to magically produce two elixirs. For each elixir, roll on the Experimental Elixir table for the elixir's effect, which is triggered when someone drinks the elixir. The elixir appears in a vial, and the vial vanishes when the elixir is drunk or poured out. If any elixir remains when you finish a XPHB, the elixir and its vial vanish.\n\nDrinking an Elixir\n\nAs a XPHB, a creature can drink the elixir or administer it to another creature within 5 feet of itself.\n\nCreating Additional Elixirs\n\nAs a XPHB action while holding XPHB, you can expend one spell slot to create another elixir. When you do so, you choose its effect from the Experimental Elixir table rather than rolling.\n\nWhen you reach certain Artificer levels, you can make an additional elixir at the end of each XPHB: a total of three at level 5, four at level 9, and five at level 15.\n\n1d6 | Effect\n\n1 | Healing. The drinker regains a number of XPHB equal to 2d8 plus your Intelligence modifier. The number of XPHB restored increases by 1d8 when you reach Artificer levels 9 (3d8) and 15 (4d8).\n\n2 | Swiftness. The drinker's XPHB increases by 10 feet for 1 hour. This bonus increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (15 feet) and 15 (20 feet).\n\n3 | Resilience. The drinker gains a +1 bonus to AC for 10 minutes. The duration increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (1 hour) and 15 (8 hours).\n\n4 | Boldness. The drinker can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to every attack roll and saving throw they make for the next minute. The duration increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (10 minutes) and 15 (1 hour).\n\n5 | Flight. The drinker gains a XPHB of 10 feet for 10 minutes. The XPHB increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (20 feet) and 15 (30 feet).\n\n6 | You determine the elixir's effect by choosing one of the other rows in this table.\n\nNivel 3 - Experimental Elixir\n\nPagina: 14\n\nBeginning at 3rd level, whenever you finish a long rest, you can magically produce an experimental elixir in an empty flask you touch. Roll on the Experimental Elixir table for the elixir's effect, which is triggered when someone drinks the elixir. As an action, a creature can drink the elixir or administer it to an incapacitated creature.\n\nCreating an experimental elixir requires you to have PHB on your person, and any elixir you create with this feature lasts until it is drunk or until the end of your next long rest.\n\nWhen you reach certain levels in this class, you can make more elixirs at the end of a long rest: two at 6th level and three at 15th level. Roll for each elixir's effect separately. Each elixir requires its own flask.\n\nYou can create additional experimental elixirs by expending a spell slot of 1st level or higher for each one. When you do so, you use your action to create the elixir in an empty flask you touch, and you choose the elixir's effect from the Experimental Elixir table.\n\nd6 | Effect\n\n1 | Healing. The drinker regains a number of hit points equal to 2d4 + your Intelligence modifier.\n\n2 | Swiftness. The drinker's walking speed increases by 10 feet for 1 hour.\n\n3 | Resilience. The drinker gains a +1 bonus to AC for 10 minutes.\n\n4 | Boldness. The drinker can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to every attack roll and saving throw they make for the next minute.\n\n5 | Flight. The drinker gains a flying speed of 10 feet for 10 minutes.\n\n6 | Transformation. The drinker's body is transformed as if by the alter self spell. The drinker determines the transformation caused by the spell, the effects of which last for 10 minutes.\n\nNivel 3 - Tool Proficiency\n\nPagina: 14\n\nWhen you adopt this specialization at 3rd level, you gain proficiency with PHB. If you already have this proficiency, you gain proficiency with one other type of PHB of your choice.\n\nNivel 3 - Tool Proficiency\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nPagina: 12\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nTool Proficiency\n\nYou gain proficiency with XPHB and the XPHB. If you already have one of these proficiencies, you gain proficiency with one other type of XPHB of your choice (or with two other types if you have both).\n\nPotion Crafting\n\nWhen you brew a potion using the crafting rules in the XDMG, the amount of time required to craft it is halved.\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nNivel 5 - Alchemical Savant\n\nPagina: 14\n\nWhenever you cast a spell using your XPHB as the XPHB, you gain a bonus to one roll of the spell. That roll must restore XPHB or be a damage roll that deals Acid, Fire, or Poison damage. The bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum bonus of +1).\n\nNivel 5 - Alchemical Savant\n\nPagina: 14\n\nAt 5th level, you develop masterful command of magical chemicals, enhancing the healing and damage you create through them. Whenever you cast a spell using your PHB as the spellcasting focus, you gain a bonus to one roll of the spell. That roll must restore hit points or be a damage roll that deals acid, fire, necrotic, or poison damage, and the bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).\n\nNivel 9 - Restorative Reagents\n\nPagina: 14\n\nYou can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot and without preparing the spell, provided you use XPHB as the XPHB. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 9 - Restorative Reagents\n\nPagina: 14\n\nStarting at 9th level, you can incorporate restorative reagents into some of your works:\n\n• Whenever a creature drinks an experimental elixir you created, the creature gains temporary hit points equal to 2d6 + your Intelligence modifier (minimum of 1 temporary hit point).\n\n• You can cast lesser restoration without expending a spell slot and without preparing the spell, provided you use PHB as the spellcasting focus. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery\n\nPagina: 14\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nAlchemical Eruption\n\nWhen you cast an Artificer spell that deals Acid, Fire, or Poison damage to a target, you can also deal 2d8 Force damage to that target. You can use this benefit only once on each of your turns.\n\nChemical Resistance\n\nYou gain XPHB to Acid damage and Poison damage. You also gain XPHB to the XPHB condition.\n\nConjured Cauldron\n\nYou can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot, without preparing the spell, and without Material components, provided you use XPHB as the XPHB. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery\n\nPagina: 14\n\nBy 15th level, you have been exposed to so many chemicals that they pose little risk to you, and you can use them to quickly end certain ailments:\n\n• You gain resistance to acid damage and poison damage, and you are immune to the poisoned condition.\n\n• You can cast greater restoration and heal without expending a spell slot, without preparing the spell, and without material components, provided you use PHB as the spellcasting focus. Once you cast either spell with this feature, you can't cast that spell with it again until you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery"},
  ["feature.alchemist.tce2014.artificer.alchemist.3"]={title="Alchemist",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 14\n\nAn Alchemist is an expert at combining reagents to produce mystical effects. Alchemists use their creations to give life and to leech it away. Alchemy is the oldest of artificer traditions, and its versatility has long been valued during times of war and peace."},
  ["feature.alchemist-spells.efa2014.artificer.alchemist.3"]={title="Alchemist Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 13\n\nWhen you reach an Artificer level specified in the Alchemist Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nArtificer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["feature.alchemist-spells.tce2014.artificer.alchemist.3"]={title="Alchemist Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 14\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Alchemist Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.\n\nArtificer Level | Spell\n\n3rd | healing word, ray of sickness\n\n5th | flaming sphere, Melf's acid arrow\n\n9th | gaseous form, mass healing word\n\n13th | blight, death ward\n\n17th | cloudkill, raise dead"},
  ["item.alchemist-s-doom.scc2014"]={title="Alchemist's Doom",subtitle="Item - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 179\n\nRaridade: unknown\n\nThis sticky, adhesive fluid ignites when exposed to air. As an action, you can throw this flask up to 20 feet, shattering it on impact. Make a ranged attack against a creature or object, treating the alchemist's doom as an improvised weapon. On a hit, the target takes 7 (2d6) fire damage at the start of each of its turns. A creature can end this damage by using its action to make a 10 Dexterity check to extinguish the flames."},
  ["item.alchemist-s-fire.xphb2024"]={title="Alchemist's Fire",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 222\n\nRaridade: none\n\nWhen you take the XPHB action, you can replace one of your attacks with throwing a flask of Alchemist's Fire. Target one creature or object you can see within 20 feet of yourself. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw (8 plus your Dexterity modifier and XPHB) or take 1d4 Fire damage and start XPHB."},
  ["item.alchemist-s-fire-flask.phb2014"]={title="Alchemist's Fire (flask)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 148\n\nRaridade: none\n\nThis sticky, adhesive fluid ignites when exposed to air. As an action, you can throw this flask up to 20 feet, shattering it on impact. Make a ranged attack against a creature or object, treating the alchemist's fire as an improvised weapon. On a hit, the target takes 1d4 fire damage at the start of each of its turns. A creature can end this damage by using its action to make a 10 Dexterity check to extinguish the flames."},
  ["item.alchemist-s-supplies.phb2014"]={title="Alchemist's Supplies",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAlchemist's supplies enable a character to produce useful concoctions, such as acid or alchemist's fire.\n\nComponents\n\nAlchemist's supplies include two glass beakers, a metal frame to hold a beaker in place over an open flame, a glass stirring rod, a small mortar and pestle, and a pouch of common alchemical ingredients, including salt, powdered iron, and purified water.\n\nArcana\n\nProficiency with alchemist's supplies allows you to unlock more information on Arcana checks involving potions and similar materials.\n\nInvestigation\n\nWhen you inspect an area for clues, proficiency with alchemist's supplies grants additional insight into any chemicals or other substances that might have been used in the area.\n\nAlchemical Crafting\n\nYou can use this tool proficiency to create alchemical items. A character can spend money to collect raw materials, which weigh 1 pound for every 50 gp spent. The DM can allow a character to make a check using the indicated skill with advantage. As part of a long rest, you can use alchemist's supplies to make one dose of phb, phb, phb, phb, phb, or phb. Subtract half the value of the created item from the total gp worth of raw materials you are carrying.\n\nActivity | DC\n\nCreate a puff of thick smoke | 10\n\nIdentify a poison | 10\n\nIdentify a substance | 15\n\nStart a fire | 15\n\nNeutralize acid | 20"},
  ["item.alchemist-s-supplies.xphb2024"]={title="Alchemist's Supplies",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 220\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Intelligence\n\n• Utilize: Identify a substance (15), or start a fire (15)\n\n• Craft: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["magicitem.alchemy-jug.dmg2014"]={title="Alchemy Jug",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis ceramic jug appears to be able to hold a gallon of liquid and weighs 12 pounds whether full or empty. Sloshing sounds can be heard from within the jug when it is shaken, even if the jug is empty.\n\nYou can use an action and name one liquid from the table below to cause the jug to produce the chosen liquid. Afterward, you can uncork the jug as an action and pour that liquid out, up to 2 gallons per minute. The maximum amount of liquid the jug can produce depends on the liquid you named.\n\nOnce the jug starts producing a liquid, it can't produce a different one, or more of one that has reached its maximum, until the next dawn.\n\nLiquid | Max Amount\n\nAcid | 8 ounces\n\nBasic poison | ½ ounce\n\nBeer | 4 gallons\n\nHoney | 1 gallon\n\nMayonnaise | 2 gallons\n\nOil | 1 quart\n\nVinegar | 2 gallons\n\nWater, fresh | 8 gallons\n\nWater, salt | 12 gallons\n\nWine | 1 gallon"},
  ["magicitem.alchemy-jug.xdmg2024"]={title="Alchemy Jug",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 227\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis ceramic jug appears to be able to hold a gallon of liquid and weighs 12 pounds whether full or empty. The jug sloshes when it is shaken, even if the jug is empty.\n\nYou can take a XPHB action and name one liquid from the Alchemy Jug Liquids table to cause the jug to produce the chosen liquid. Afterward, you can uncork the jug as a XPHB action and pour that liquid out, up to 2 gallons per minute. The maximum amount of liquid the jug can produce depends on the liquid you named.\n\nOnce the jug starts producing a liquid, it can't produce a different one, or more of one that has reached its maximum, until the next dawn.\n\nLiquid | Max. Amount\n\nAcid | 8 ounces\n\nBasic Poison | 4 ounces\n\nBeer | 4 gallons\n\nHoney | 1 gallon\n\nMayonnaise | 2 gallons\n\nOil | 1 quart\n\nVinegar | 2 gallons\n\nWater, fresh | 8 gallons\n\nWater, salt | 12 gallons\n\nWine | 1 gallon\n\nreplicate magic item|artificer|efa|2|efa"},
  ["magicitem.alchemy-jug-blue.cm2014"]={title="Alchemy Jug (Blue)",subtitle="Item Magico - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis ceramic jug appears to be able to hold a gallon of liquid and weighs 12 pounds whether full or empty. Sloshing sounds can be heard from within the jug when it is shaken, even if the jug is empty.\n\nYou can use an action and name one liquid from the table below to cause the jug to produce the chosen liquid. Afterward, you can uncork the jug as an action and pour that liquid out, up to 2 gallons per minute. The maximum amount of liquid the jug can produce depends on the liquid you named.\n\nOnce the jug starts producing a liquid, it can't produce a different one, or more of one that has reached its maximum, until the next dawn.\n\nLiquid | Max Amount\n\nBeer | 4 gallons\n\nBoiling Hot Tea | 1 quart\n\nHoney | 1 gallon\n\nMayonnaise | 2 gallons\n\nOil | 1 quart\n\nVinegar | 2 gallons\n\nWater, fresh | 8 gallons\n\nWater, salt | 12 gallons\n\nWine | 1 gallon"},
  ["magicitem.alchemy-jug-orange.cm2014"]={title="Alchemy Jug (Orange)",subtitle="Item Magico - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis ceramic jug appears to be able to hold a gallon of liquid and weighs 12 pounds whether full or empty. Sloshing sounds can be heard from within the jug when it is shaken, even if the jug is empty.\n\nYou can use an action and name one liquid from the table below to cause the jug to produce the chosen liquid. Afterward, you can uncork the jug as an action and pour that liquid out, up to 2 gallons per minute. The maximum amount of liquid the jug can produce depends on the liquid you named.\n\nOnce the jug starts producing a liquid, it can't produce a different one, or more of one that has reached its maximum, until the next dawn.\n\nLiquid | Max Amount\n\nBeer | 4 gallons\n\nHoney | 1 gallon\n\nMayonnaise | 2 gallons\n\nOil | 1 quart\n\nSoy Sauce | 1 gallon\n\nVinegar | 2 gallons\n\nWater, fresh | 8 gallons\n\nWater, salt | 12 gallons\n\nWine | 1 gallon"},
  ["creature.aldani-lobsterfolk.toa2014"]={title="Aldani (Lobsterfolk)",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 49 (9d8 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 8 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe aldani can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe aldani makes two attacks with its claws.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d8 + 1) slashing damage, and the target is grappled (escape 11). The aldani has two claws, each of which can grapple only one target."},
  ["item.ale-gallon.phb2014"]={title="Ale (gallon)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 158\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.ale-mug.phb2014"]={title="Ale (mug)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 158\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.ale-mug.xphb2024"]={title="Ale (mug)",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 231\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["feat.alert.phb2014"]={title="Alert",subtitle="Feat - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 165\n\nAlways on the lookout for danger, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• You gain a +5 bonus to initiative.\n\n• You can't be surprised while you are conscious.\n\n• Other creatures don't gain advantage on attack rolls against you as a result of being unseen by you."},
  ["feat.alert.xphb2024"]={title="Alert",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 200\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nInitiative Proficiency\n\nWhen you roll XPHB, you can add your XPHB to the roll.\n\nInitiative Swap\n\nImmediately after you roll XPHB, you can swap your XPHB with the XPHB of one willing ally in the same combat. You can't make this swap if you or the ally has the XPHB condition."},
  ["item.alexandrite.dmg2014"]={title="Alexandrite",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent dark green gemstone."},
  ["item.alexandrite.xdmg2024"]={title="Alexandrite",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA dark green gemstone."},
  ["creature.alhoon.mpmm2014"]={title="Alhoon",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 150 (20d8 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 15\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 19 | WIS 17 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, Undercommon, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, lightning, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe alhoon has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nTurn Resistance\n\nThe alhoon has advantage on saving throws against any effect that turns Undead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe alhoon makes two Chilling Grasp or Arcane Bolt attacks.\n\nChilling Grasp\n\nms 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (4d6) cold damage, and the alhoon regains 14 hit points.\n\nArcane Bolt\n\nrs 8 to hit, range 120 ft., one target. h28 (8d6) force damage.\n\nMind Blast {@recharge 5}\n\nThe alhoon magically emits psychic energy in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 16 Intelligence saving throw or take 22 (4d8 + 4) psychic damage and be stunned for 1 minute. A target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nNegate Spell (3/Day)\n\nThe alhoon targets one creature it can see within 60 feet of it that is casting a spell. If the spell is 3rd level or lower, the spell fails, but any spell slots or charges are not wasted."},
  ["creature.alhoon.vgm2014"]={title="Alhoon",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 172\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 120 (16d8 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 19 | WIS 17 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, Undercommon, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, lightning, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe alhoon has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nTurn Resistance\n\nThe alhoon has advantage on saving throws against any effect that turns undead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Psionics)\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nChilling Grasp\n\nms 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (3d6) cold damage.\n\nMind Blast {@recharge 5}\n\nThe alhoon magically emits psychic energy in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 16 Intelligence saving throw or take 22 (4d8 + 4) psychic damage and be stunned for 1 minute. A target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.aljanor-keenblade.oota2014"]={title="Aljanor Keenblade",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nCA: 10"},
  ["creature.alkilith.mpmm2014"]={title="Alkilith",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 168 (16d8 + 96)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 19 | CON 22 | INT 6 | WIS 11 | CHA 7\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAbyssal Rift\n\nIf the alkilith surrounds a door, window, or similar opening continuously for 6d6 days, the opening becomes a permanent portal to a random layer of the Abyss.\n\nAmorphous\n\nThe alkilith can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nIf the alkilith is motionless at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the alkilith move or act, that creature must succeed on a 18 Intelligence (Investigation) check to discern that the alkilith isn't ordinary slime or fungus.\n\nFoment Confusion\n\nAny creature that isn't a demon that starts its turn within 30 feet of the alkilith must succeed on a 18 Wisdom saving throw, or it hears a faint buzzing in its head for a moment and has disadvantage on its next attack roll, saving throw, or ability check.\n\nIf the saving throw against Foment Confusion fails by 5 or more, the creature is instead subjected to the confusion spell for 1 minute (no concentration required by the alkilith). While under the effect of that confusion, the creature is immune to Foment Confusion.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe alkilith has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe alkilith can climb difficult surfaces, such as upside down on ceilings, without making an ability check.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe alkilith doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe alkilith makes three Tentacle attacks.\n\nTentacle\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h18 (4d6 + 4) acid damage."},
  ["creature.alkilith.mtf2014"]={title="Alkilith",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 130\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 157 (15d8 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 19 | CON 22 | INT 6 | WIS 11 | CHA 7\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmorphous\n\nThe alkilith can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the alkilith is motionless, it is indistinguishable from an ordinary slime or fungus.\n\nFoment Madness\n\nAny creature that isn't a demon that starts its turn within 30 feet of the alkilith must succeed on a 18 Wisdom saving throw, or it hears a faint buzzing in its head for a moment and has disadvantage on its next attack roll, saving throw, or ability check.\n\nIf the saving throw against Foment Madness fails by 5 or more, the creature is instead subjected to the confusion spell for 1 minute (no concentration required by the alkilith). While under the effect of that confusion, the creature is immune to Foment Madness.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe alkilith has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe alkilith makes three tentacle attacks.\n\nTentacle\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h18 (4d6 + 4) acid damage."},
  ["creature.allip.mpmm2014"]={title="Allip",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 45\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 40 (9d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 40\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 17 | CON 10 | INT 17 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: the languages it knew in life\n\nResistencias: acid, fire, lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades: cold, necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nThe allip can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe allip doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMaddening Touch\n\nms 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (4d6 + 3) psychic damage.\n\nHowling Babble {@recharge}\n\nEach creature within 30 feet of the allip that can hear it must make a 14 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, a target takes 12 (2d8 + 3) psychic damage, and it is stunned until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and isn't stunned. Constructs and Undead are immune to this effect.\n\nWhispers of Compulsion\n\nThe allip chooses up to three creatures it can see within 60 feet of it. Each target must succeed on a 14 Wisdom saving throw, or it takes 12 (2d8 + 3) psychic damage and must use its reaction to make a melee weapon attack against one creature of the allip's choice that the allip can see. Constructs and Undead are immune to this effect."},
  ["creature.allip.mtf2014"]={title="Allip",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 40 (9d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 40\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 17 | CON 10 | INT 17 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: the languages it knew in life\n\nResistencias: acid, fire, lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades: cold, necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nThe allip can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMaddening Touch\n\nms 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (4d6 + 3) psychic damage.\n\nWhispers of Madness\n\nThe allip chooses up to three creatures it can see within 60 feet of it. Each target must succeed on a 14 Wisdom saving throw, or it takes 7 (1d8 + 3) psychic damage and must use its reaction to make a melee weapon attack against one creature of the allip's choice that the allip can see. Constructs and undead are immune to this effect.\n\nHowling Babble {@recharge}\n\nEach creature within 30 feet of the allip that can hear it must make a 14 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, a target takes 12 (2d8 + 3) psychic damage, and it is stunned until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and isn't stunned. Constructs and undead are immune to this effect."},
  ["creature.allosaurus.mm2014"]={title="Allosaurus",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 79\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 51 (6d10 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 13 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 12 | CHA 5\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPounce\n\nIf the allosaurus moves at least 30 feet straight toward a creature and then hits it with a claw attack on the same turn, that target must succeed on a 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone. If the target is prone, the allosaurus can make one bite attack against it as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.allosaurus.xmm2024"]={title="Allosaurus",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 348\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 51 (6d10 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 13 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 12 | CHA 5\n\nPericias: \n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h15 (2d10 + 4) Piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature and the allosaurus moved 30+ feet straight toward it immediately before the hit, the target has the XPHB condition, and the allosaurus can make one Bite attack against it."},
  ["creature.allowak-abominable-yeti.egw2014"]={title="Allowak Abominable Yeti",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 126\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 16 | CHA 10\n\nIdiomas: Common, Yeti"},
  ["creature.allowak-yeti.egw2014"]={title="Allowak Yeti",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 126\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 16 | CHA 10\n\nIdiomas: Common, Yeti"},
  ["creature.almiraj.toa2014"]={title="Almiraj",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / S\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 3 (1d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 2 | DEX 16 | CON 10 | INT 2 | WIS 14 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Senses\n\nThe almiraj has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or sight.\n\nFamiliar\n\nWith the DM's permission, the find familiar spell can summon an almiraj.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHorn\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["deity.alobal-lorfiril.mtf2014"]={title="Alobal Lorfiril",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43"},
  ["creature.aloysia-telfan.crcotn2014"]={title="Aloysia Telfan",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 61\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M"},
  ["creature.alseid.mot2014"]={title="Alseid",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 235\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 10 | CON 12 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 18\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: radiant\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHide in Plain Sight\n\nThe alseid has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide while it is in grassland.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe alseid has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe alseid makes two radiant touch attacks.\n\nRadiant Touch\n\nms 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) radiant damage."},
  ["feature.alter-memories.au2014.wizard.enchanter.14"]={title="Alter Memories",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.alter-memories.phb2014.wizard.enchantment.14"]={title="Alter Memories",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 117\n\nAt 14th level, you gain the ability to make a creature unaware of your magical influence on it. When you cast an enchantment spell to charm one or more creatures, you can alter one creature's understanding so that it remains unaware of being charmed.\n\nAdditionally, once before the spell expires, you can use your action to try to make the chosen creature forget some of the time it spent charmed. The creature must succeed on an Intelligence saving throw against your wizard spell save DC or lose a number of hours of its memories equal to 1 + your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1). You can make the creature forget less time, and the amount of time can't exceed the duration of your enchantment spell."},
  ["spell.alter-self.phb2014"]={title="Alter Self",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\nYou assume a different form. When you cast the spell, choose one of the following options, the effects of which last for the duration of the spell. While the spell lasts, you can end one option as an action to gain the benefits of a different one.\n\nAquatic Adaptation\n\nYou adapt your body to an aquatic environment, sprouting gills and growing webbing between your fingers. You can breathe underwater and gain a swimming speed equal to your walking speed.\n\nChange Appearance\n\nYou transform your appearance. You decide what you look like, including your height, weight, facial features, sound of your voice, hair length, coloration, and distinguishing characteristics, if any. You can make yourself appear as a member of another race, though none of your statistics change. You also can't appear as a creature of a different size than you, and your basic shape stays the same; if you're bipedal, you can't use this spell to become quadrupedal, for instance. At any time for the duration of the spell, you can use your action to change your appearance in this way again.\n\nNatural Weapons\n\nYou grow claws, fangs, spines, horns, or a different natural weapon of your choice. Your unarmed strikes deal 1d6 bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage, as appropriate to the natural weapon you chose, and you are proficient with your unarmed strikes. Finally, the natural weapon is magic and you have a +1 bonus to the attack and damage rolls you make using it."},
  ["spell.alter-self.xphb2024"]={title="Alter Self",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 239\n\nYou alter your physical form. Choose one of the following options. Its effects last for the duration, during which you can take a XPHB action to replace the option you chose with a different one.\n\nAquatic Adaptation\n\nYou sprout gills and grow webs between your fingers. You can breathe underwater and gain a XPHB equal to your XPHB.\n\nChange Appearance\n\nYou alter your appearance. You decide what you look like, including your height, weight, facial features, sound of your voice, hair length, coloration, and other distinguishing characteristics. You can make yourself appear as a member of another species, though none of your statistics change. You can't appear as a creature of a different size, and your basic shape stays the same; if you're bipedal, you can't use this spell to become quadrupedal, for instance. For the duration, you can take a XPHB action to change your appearance in this way again.\n\nNatural Weapons\n\nYou grow claws (Slashing), fangs (Piercing), horns (Piercing), or hooves (Bludgeoning). When you use your XPHB to deal damage with that new growth, it deals 1d6 damage of the type in parentheses instead of dealing the normal damage for your XPHB, and you use your spellcasting ability modifier for the attack and damage rolls rather than using Strength."},
  ["creature.altisaur.bgg2014"]={title="Altisaur",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 129\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / G\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 198 (12d20 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 6 | CON 23 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe altisaur has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe altisaur makes one Stomp attack and one Tail attack. The altisaur can't make both attacks against the same target.\n\nStomp\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h33 (7d6 + 9) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 22 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nTail\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h45 (8d8 + 9) bludgeoning damage, and the target is pushed up to 20 feet horizontally from the altisaur."},
  ["creature.altisaur.psx2014"]={title="Altisaur",subtitle="Criatura - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.alustriel-silverhand.veor2014"]={title="Alustriel Silverhand",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 242\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 15/18\n\nPV: 272 (32d8 + 128)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 20 | CON 18 | INT 24 | WIS 23 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Elvish\n\nResistencias: radiant\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEar of the Chosen\n\nWhenever a creature on the same plane of existence as Alustriel speaks Alustriel's name, Alustriel hears her name and the next nine words the speaker utters.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Alustriel fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nAlustriel carries a magic staff known as the Staff of Silverymoon. In the hands of anyone other than Alustriel, the Staff of Silverymoon is a Staff of Power.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAlustriel makes three Staff of Silverymoon attacks or two Reproving Ray attacks.\n\nStaff of Silverymoon\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage plus 38 (7d10) radiant damage.\n\nReproving Ray\n\nrs 14 to hit, range 120 ft., one target. h65 (9d12 + 7) force damage, and if the target is a creature, it must make a 22 Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, the target has the incapacitated condition until the start of Alustriel's next turn. On a successful save, the target's speed is reduced by 10 feet until the start of Alustriel's next turn.\n\nArgent Blaze (Requires Silver Fire)\n\nAlustriel summons a 60-foot cone of silver fire. Each creature in that area must make a 22 Dexterity saving throw, taking 77 (14d10) radiant damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. Additionally, Alustriel or one creature of her choice within 60 feet of her then regains 10 (3d6) hit points.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nSilver Fire (2/Day)\n\nBrilliant silver fire harmlessly wreathes Alustriel and empowers her. The silver fire lasts for 1 hour or until she has the incapacitated condition or uses another bonus action to quench it. While wreathed in silver fire, Alustriel gains truesight within 30 feet and can use her Argent Blaze action. In addition, Alustriel is unaffected by magic that would ascertain her alignment, creature type, thoughts, or truthfulness.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nShining Counterspell\n\nAlustriel interrupts a creature she can see within 60 feet of herself that is casting a spell. If the spell is 5th level or lower, it fails and has no effect. If the spell is 6th level or higher, Alustriel makes an Intelligence check (10 plus the spell's level). On a successful check, the spell fails and has no effect. Whatever the spell's level, the caster takes 11 (2d10) radiant damage if the spell fails."},
  ["spell.alustriel-s-mooncloak.frhof2014"]={title="Alustriel's Mooncloak",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 142\n\nFor the duration, moonlight fills a 20-foot XPHB originating from you with XPHB. While in that area, you and your allies have XPHB and XPHB to Cold, Lightning, and Radiant damage.\n\nWhile the spell lasts, you can use one of the following options, ending the spell immediately:\n\n• Liberation When you fail a saving throw to avoid or end the XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB condition, you can take a XPHB to succeed on the save instead.\n\n• Respite As a XPHB action, you or an ally within the area regains XPHB equal to 4d10 plus your spellcasting ability modifier."},
  ["creature.alyxian-aboleth.crcotn2014"]={title="Alyxian Aboleth",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 195\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 135 (18d10 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, swim: 30\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 9 | CON 15 | INT 18 | WIS 18 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, telepathy 120 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe aboleth can breathe air and water.\n\nMucous Cloud\n\nWhile underwater, the aboleth is surrounded by a cloud of sticky mucus. A creature that touches the aboleth or hits it with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be restrained until the end of the aboleth's next turn.\n\nProbing Telepathy\n\nIf a creature the aboleth can see communicates telepathically with the aboleth, the aboleth learns the creature's greatest desires.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe aboleth makes two Tentacle attacks.\n\nTentacle\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) psychic damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEnslave {@recharge 4}\n\nThe aboleth targets one creature it can see within 30 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 14 Wisdom saving throw or be magically charmed by the aboleth until the aboleth dies or until it is on a different plane of existence from the target. The charmed target is under the aboleth's control and can't take reactions, and the aboleth and the target can communicate telepathically with each other over any distance.\n\nThe charmed target can repeat the saving throw whenever it takes damage, ending the effect on itself on a success. No more than once every 24 hours, the target can repeat the saving throw when it is at least 1 mile away from the aboleth.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTail Swipe\n\nThe aboleth makes one Tail attack.\n\nPsychic Drain (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nOne creature charmed by the aboleth takes 10 (3d6) psychic damage, and the aboleth regains hit points equal to the damage dealt."},
  ["creature.alyxian-the-absolved.crcotn2014"]={title="Alyxian the Absolved",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 182\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 161 (19d8 + 76)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 15 | CON 18 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDivinely Blessed\n\nAlyxian can't be surprised and can't be changed into another form against his will.\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf Alyxian fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAlyxian makes two Spear attacks.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage, or 8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage when used with two hands to make a melee attack, plus 9 (2d8) radiant damage.\n\nForce Wave (1/Day)\n\nAlyxian strikes the ground, creating a burst of energy that ripples outward. Each creature he chooses within a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on himself must succeed on a 17 Constitution saving throw or take 35 (10d6) force damage and be knocked prone. A creature that succeeds on the saving throw takes half as much damage and isn't knocked prone.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nAlyxian adds 3 to his AC against one attack roll that would hit him. To do so, Alyxian must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nArch Heart's Strike\n\nAlyxian makes one Spear attack, and all damage from this attack is radiant.\n\nChange Bringer's Dance\n\nAlyxian moves up to his speed. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks.\n\nMoon Weaver's Veil (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nAlyxian becomes invisible until the end of his next turn. Any equipment he is wearing or carrying becomes invisible with him."},
  ["creature.alyxian-the-callous.crcotn2014"]={title="Alyxian the Callous",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 179\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / L\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 157 (15d10 + 75)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 90\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 18 | CON 21 | INT 15 | WIS 16 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Elvish, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nImunidades: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, restrained, stunned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nApotheonic Rejuvenation\n\nWhen Alyxian the Callous drops to 0 hit points, his body dies and sheds its wings, and he rises to his feet in his third form, Alyxian the Dispossessed. His initiative count doesn't change.\n\nDivinely Blessed\n\nAlyxian can't be surprised and can't be changed into another form against his will.\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf Alyxian fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAlyxian makes two Radiant Spear attacks. He can replace one of these attacks with Blinding Teleport.\n\nRadiant Spear\n\nmw,rw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h15 (2d8 + 6) radiant damage.\n\nBlinding Teleport\n\nAlyxian teleports, along with any equipment he is wearing or carrying, to an unoccupied space he can see within 120 feet of himself. Each creature within 5 feet of his new location must succeed on a 17 Constitution saving throw or be blinded until the end of its next turn.\n\nHeavenly Destruction (1/Day)\n\nAlyxian releases divine energy in a 60-foot cone. Each creature of his choice in that area must make a 17 Constitution saving throw. On a failed saving throw, the creature takes 31 (7d8) radiant damage and is knocked prone. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage and isn't knocked prone.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nAlyxian makes one Radiant Spear attack.\n\nCelestial Chains\n\nAlyxian targets one creature he can see within 120 feet of himself. The target must succeed on a 17 Strength saving throw or be restrained by magical chains for 1 minute. While restrained in this way, the target can't leave the space by any means. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nFlare (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nAlyxian targets one creature he can see within 30 feet of himself. Light flares around the target, dealing 17 (5d6) radiant damage to it and creatures within 10 feet of it."},
  ["creature.alyxian-the-dispossessed.crcotn2014"]={title="Alyxian the Dispossessed",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 180\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 153 (18d8 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 15 | CON 18 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Elvish, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, stunned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDivinely Blessed\n\nAlyxian can't be surprised and can't be changed into another form against his will.\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf Alyxian fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nAlyxian carries a magic dagger that he uses to make Stoneheart Dagger attacks. In the hands of creatures other than Alyxian, the dagger is nonmagical and has no special properties.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAlyxian makes two Spear attacks.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage, or 8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage when used with two hands to make a melee attack, plus 9 (2d8) radiant damage.\n\nStoneheart Dagger\n\nmw,rw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h11 (3d4 + 4) force damage, and if the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 17 Constitution saving throw or become petrified as the dagger lodges itself in the target's body. While the dagger is lodged in the target, magic can't end the petrified condition on it and Alyxian can't make Stoneheart Dagger attacks. A creature within reach of the petrified target can use an action to try to remove the dagger, doing so with a successful 17 Strength check.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nSummon Dagger\n\nAlyxian's Stoneheart Dagger teleports into his free hand, provided he has one.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nAlyxian adds 3 to his AC against one attack roll that would hit him. To do so, Alyxian must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nAlyxian makes one Spear or Stoneheart Dagger attack.\n\nWarrior's Stride\n\nAlyxian moves up to his speed. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks.\n\nRuidium Shard (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nA gem-sized shard of ruidium appears at a point Alyxian can see within 120 feet of himself and explodes. Each creature, other than Alyxian, in a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must succeed on a 18 Charisma saving throw or gain 1 level of exhaustion. If a creature isn't suffering from ruidium corruption, it becomes corrupted when it fails the saving throw."},
  ["creature.alyxian-the-hunter.crcotn2014"]={title="Alyxian the Hunter",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 160\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 178 (17d10 + 85)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 9 | CON 20 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe golem is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe golem has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe golem's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe golem makes two slam attacks.\n\nRuidium Dart\n\nThe golem can conjure a magic dart made of ruidium and hurl it at another creature it can see within 120 feet of itself. The dart strikes the target unerringly and vanishes on contact. The target must make a 17 Charisma saving throw. On a failed saving throw, the target takes 24 (7d6) psychic damage and gains 1 level of exhaustion. In addition, if the target is not already suffering from ruidium corruption, it becomes corrupted when it fails the saving throw. On a successful saving throw, the target takes half as much damage and suffers no other effects.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h19 (3d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nSlow {@recharge 5}\n\nThe golem targets one or more creatures it can see within 10 feet of it. Each target must make a 17 Wisdom saving throw against this magic. On a failed save, a target can't use reactions, its speed is halved, and it can't make more than one attack on its turn. In addition, the target can take either an action or a bonus action on its turn, not both. These effects last for 1 minute. A target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.alyxian-the-tormented.crcotn2014"]={title="Alyxian the Tormented",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 178\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / H\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 150 (12d12 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, swim: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 18 | CON 22 | INT 15 | WIS 16 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Elvish, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nImunidades: necrotic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, stunned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nApotheonic Rejuvenation\n\nWhen Alyxian drops to 0 hit points, his body dies and cracks open like a cocoon. Alyxian instantly emerges from the cocoon in his second form, Alyxian the Callous, in the space where his previous form died. His initiative count doesn't change.\n\nDivinely Blessed\n\nAlyxian can't be surprised and can't be changed into another form against his will.\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf Alyxian fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAlyxian makes two Grasping Hand attacks.\n\nGrasping Hand\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (3d6 + 5) force damage, and if the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 15). Alyxian has six hands, each of which can grapple one target.\n\nVoid Eyes {@recharge 5}\n\nAlyxian targets up to two creatures he can see within 120 feet of himself. Each target must make a 17 Constitution saving throw, taking 28 (8d6) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nAlyxian makes one Grasping Hand attack.\n\nWeapons of Yore (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nAncient weapons embedded in Alyxian's hide detach from Alyxian and fly about in a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on a point Alyxian can see within 60 feet of himself. A creature takes 18 (4d8) slashing damage when it enters that area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there. The effect lasts until the end of Alyxian's next turn, when the weapons return to Alyxian and embed themselves in his hide once again (causing him no harm)."},
  ["language.alzhedo.frhof2014"]={title="Alzhedo",subtitle="Idioma - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 49"},
  ["language.alzhedo.scag2014"]={title="Alzhedo",subtitle="Idioma - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\nOption: Human Languages\n\nMany human ethnicities and nations in Faerûn have their own language, in addition to Common. Most human languages are written in Thorass, the alphabet of Old Common, derived from the Chondathan language that traders used as their common tongue. A few human languages use other alphabets, including Draconic, Dethek, and Espruar.\n\nIf your Dungeon Master allows this option, then any human from an ethnic group that has its own language is assumed to know that language as well as Common. This ethnic language is treated as a free additional language for such individuals."},
  ["creature.amanisha-manivarshi.jttrc2014"]={title="Amanisha Manivarshi",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 127\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.amarith-coppervein.oota2014"]={title="Amarith Coppervein",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 142\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["deity.amaunator.frhof2014"]={title="Amaunator",subtitle="Divindade - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 100\n\nThe rule of law and the glory of the sun both fall in Amaunator's dominion. He is a stern and unforgiving god, concerned with keeping promises and maintaining order.\n\nAmaunator's followers believe he has died and been reborn time and again. They quarrel with followers of Lathander over whether Lathander is an aspect of Amaunator or is a separate deity. Either way, Lathander represents the optimistic light of dawn, while Amaunator represents the sun in all aspects. At times, the sun is warm and encouraging; at others, harsh and unforgiving. What matters most is that it reliably rises each day and sets each night.\n\nWhen Amaunator sends a messenger, its presence is unmistakable: a XMM or a seemingly ordinary bird with gleaming eyes like miniature suns descends from the heavens in a shaft of bright light. Amaunator also communicates with his followers via dreams in which the darkness of night is suddenly vanquished by the broad daylight.\n\nThe folk of Faerûn invoke Amaunator's name when praying for sunny weather, swearing oaths, signing contracts, and declaring laws. The connection between a solemn oath and the light of the sun is ingrained in the people of Faerûn; those closing deals or issuing edicts often pause and wait for a passing cloud to clear the sun before completing the transaction or pronouncement.\n\nAmaunator's priests help establish bureaucracies and order in communities. They witness contracts and signed agreements, signifying these documents' validity by stamping them with the god's sun symbol. Temples to Amaunator feature courtyards and skylights to invite the god's bright gaze. In underground settlements or places plagued by cloud cover, his temples mount a torch with a XPHB spell cast on it over their doorway to symbolize the sun. Amaunator's temples keep extensive records of their surrounding community's laws and legal proceedings. Most temples make these records available to the public for transparency. In places where corruption has spread even to Amaunator's temples, access to these records cost a hefty sum.\n\nThe Chosen of Amaunator master magic that dispels darkness and unveils hidden truths. Some work to enforce the law across the land; others become magistrates in Faerûn's highest courts."},
  ["deity.amaunator.scag2014"]={title="Amaunator",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nThe rule of law and the glory of the sun are both in Amaunator's dominion. His priests help establish bureaucracies and lawful order in communities. They often witness contracts and signed agreements, stamping such documents with the sun-symbol of Amaunator to signify their validity.\n\nHis priests teach that Amaunator has died and been reborn time and again. Like the sun, he might pass into the realm of darkness, but inevitably his bright gaze will fall on the world once again. Amaunator is seen as a stern and unforgiving deity, not unlike Silvanus in comportment, but his concern isn't for the balance of life - he cares that things proceed according to the celestial order, that promises are kept, and that the rule of law persists.\n\nFarmers and travelers beseech him when they pray for rain or sun, as do any others looking for a favorable change in the weather. But the most common form of propitiation to Amaunator is the practice of swearing oaths, signing contracts, and declaring laws under the light of the sun. So ingrained in the common perception is the connection between a solemn oath and the sun that those engaged in closing deals or issuing edicts often pause and wait for a passing cloud to clear the sun before completing the transaction or pronouncement."},
  ["item.amber.dmg2014"]={title="Amber",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent watery gold to rich gold gemstone."},
  ["item.amber.xdmg2024"]={title="Amber",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA watery gold to rich gold gemstone."},
  ["creature.amber-golem.cos2014"]={title="Amber Golem",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 186\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["magicitem.amber-runestone.nrh-tlt2014"]={title="Amber Runestone",subtitle="Item Magico - NRH-TLT - 2014",body="Pagina: 6\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis piece of polished amber is engraved with many tiny runes. As a bonus action, you can mentally command the stone to shed bright light in a 15-foot radius and dim light for an additional 15 feet. The light is sunlight. While the light persists, you can also use a bonus action to expand or reduce its radius of bright and dim light by 5 feet each, to a maximum of 30 feet each or a minimum of 10 feet each."},
  ["subclass.ambition-domain-psa.psa2014.cleric.ambition-psa.0"]={title="Ambition Domain (PSA)",subtitle="Subclasse - PSA - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Ambition Domain (PSA)\n\nPagina: 27\n\nThe worthy shall strive for greatness—supremacy in life leads to supremacy in the afterlife.\n\nBontu has fully embraced this dictum, and though she expends little effort in teaching it, she surely leads by example. Her viziers subtly plant the seeds that flower into the ambition the God-Pharaoh desires. Through insinuation, they remind acolytes and initiates alike that achieving one's place in the afterlife at the expense of others is not shameful, but is proof of the initiate's determination and drive. Nothing is more important than that drive, they suggest—not the bonds of a crop, not friendship or love. Not even devotion to a deity.\n\nAt each indicated cleric level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | bane, disguise self\n\n3rd | mirror image, ray of enfeeblement\n\n5th | bestow curse, vampiric touch\n\n7th | death ward, dimension door\n\n9th | dominate person, modify memory\n\nNivel 1 - Warding Flare\n\nPagina: 27\n\nWhen you choose this domain at 1st level, you can interpose divine light between yourself and an attacking enemy. When you are attacked by a creature within 30 feet of you that you can see, you can use your reaction to impose disadvantage on the attack roll, causing light to flare before the attacker before it hits or misses. An attacker that can't be blinded is immune to this feature.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 2 - Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity\n\nPagina: 27\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to create an illusory duplicate of yourself.\n\nAs an action, you create a perfect illusion of yourself that lasts for 1 minute, or until you lose your concentration (as if you were concentration on a spell). The illusion appears in an unoccupied space that you can see within 30 feet of you. As a bonus action on your turn, you can move the illusion up to 30 feet to a space you can see, but it must remain within 120 feet of you.\n\nFor the duration, you can cast spells as though you were in the illusion's space, but you must use your own senses. Additionally, when both you and your illusion are within 5 feet of a creature that can see the illusion, you have advantage on attack rolls against that creature, given how distracting the illusion is to the target.\n\nNivel 3 - Ambition Domain (PSA)\n\nNivel 3 - Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity\n\nNivel 6 - Channel Divinity: Cloak of Shadows\n\nPagina: 27\n\nStarting at 6th level, you can use your Channel Divinity to vanish. As an action, you become invisible until the end of your next turn. You become visible if you attack or cast a spell.\n\nNivel 8 - Blessed Strikes\n\nPagina: 30\n\n{@i 8th-level cleric tce, which replaces the Potent Spellcasting feature\n\nYou are blessed with divine might in battle. When a creature takes damage from one of your cantrips or weapon attacks, you can also deal 1d8 radiant damage to that creature. Once you deal this damage, you can't use this feature again until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 8 - Potent Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 27\n\nStarting at 8th level, you add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any cleric cantrip.\n\nNivel 17 - Improved Duplicity\n\nPagina: 27\n\nAt 17th level, you can create up to four duplicates of yourself, instead of one, when you use Invoke Duplicity. As a bonus action on your turn, you can move any number of them up to 30 feet, to a maximum range of 120 feet."},
  ["feature.ambition-domain-psa.psa2014.cleric.ambition-psa.1"]={title="Ambition Domain (PSA)",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nThe worthy shall strive for greatness—supremacy in life leads to supremacy in the afterlife.\n\nBontu has fully embraced this dictum, and though she expends little effort in teaching it, she surely leads by example. Her viziers subtly plant the seeds that flower into the ambition the God-Pharaoh desires. Through insinuation, they remind acolytes and initiates alike that achieving one's place in the afterlife at the expense of others is not shameful, but is proof of the initiate's determination and drive. Nothing is more important than that drive, they suggest—not the bonds of a crop, not friendship or love. Not even devotion to a deity.\n\nAt each indicated cleric level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | bane, disguise self\n\n3rd | mirror image, ray of enfeeblement\n\n5th | bestow curse, vampiric touch\n\n7th | death ward, dimension door\n\n9th | dominate person, modify memory"},
  ["feature.ambition-domain-psa.psa2014.cleric.ambition-psa.3"]={title="Ambition Domain (PSA)",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.ambitious-assassin.bmt2014"]={title="Ambitious Assassin",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 45\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 91 (14d8 + 28)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 18 | CON 15 | INT 18 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, thieves' cant, plus any one language\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf the assassin fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe assassin makes two Poison Blade attacks.\n\nPoison Blade\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) piercing damage plus 5 (1d10) poison damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUncanny Dodge\n\nWhen an attacker the assassin can see hits the assassin with an attack, the assassin halves the attack's damage against it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCunning\n\nThe assassin escapes nonmagical restraints and ends the grappled condition on itself, then moves up to its speed without provoking opportunity attacks.\n\nStab (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe assassin makes one Poison Blade attack.\n\nVanishing Escape (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe assassin creates a sudden distraction, such as a cloud of disorienting smoke or flash of dazzling light, filling a 10-foot cube within 5 feet of the assassin. Each creature of the assassin's choice in that area takes 9 (2d8) psychic damage, and the assassin has the invisible condition. This invisibility lasts until the end of the assassin's next turn."},
  ["creature.amble.lr2014"]={title="Amble",subtitle="Criatura - LR - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 90 (12d8 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 18 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Aquan, Common, Druidic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHearth of Moonlight and Shadow\n\nAt the start of a short or long rest, Amble can touch a point in space, and an invisible, 30-foot-radius sphere of magic appears, centered on that point. Cover blocks the sphere.\n\nWhile within the sphere, Amble and their allies gain a +5 bonus to Dexterity (Stealth) and Wisdom (Perception) checks, and any light from open flames in the sphere isn't visible outside it.\n\nThe sphere vanishes at the end of the rest or when Amble leaves the sphere.\n\nHold Breath\n\nAmble can hold their breath for up to 1 hour at a time.\n\nBalm of the Summer Court (12d6)\n\n(As a Bonus Action) Amble can choose one creature they can see within 120 feet of them and spend up to 6d6 of their die pool. Roll the spent dice and add them together. The target regains a number of hit points equal to the total. The target also gains 1 temporary hit point per die spent. Amble regains all expended dice when they finish a long rest.\n\nHidden Paths (4/Day)\n\n(As a Bonus Action) Amble may teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space they can see.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nChange Shape (2/Day)\n\nAmble magically polymorphs into a beast with a challenge rating of 1 or less, and can remain in this form for up to 6 hours. Amble's equipment melds with their new form. Amble reverts to their true form if they die or fall unconscious. Amble can revert to their true form using a bonus action on their turn.\n\nAmble's game statistics are replaced by the statistics of the beast, but they retain their alignment, personality, and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores. Amble also retains all their skill and saving throw proficiencies, in addition to gaining those of the creature. If the creature has the same proficiency as Amble and the bonus in its stat block is higher, use the creature's bonus instead of Amble's.\n\nWhen Amble transforms, they assume the beast's hit points and Hit Dice. When Amble reverts to their normal form, they return to the number of hit points they had before they transformed. However, if Amble reverts as a result of dropping to 0 hit points, any excess damage carries over their normal form.\n\nAmble can't cast spells, and their ability to speak or take any action that requires hands is limited to the capabilities of their beast form. Transforming doesn't break Amble's concentration on a spell they've already cast however, or prevent them from taking actions that are part of a spell.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nClub\n\nmw 6 to hit (8 to hit with shillelagh), reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage, or 8 (1d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage with shillelagh."},
  ["optionalfeature.ambush.tce2014"]={title="Ambush",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nWhen you make a Dexterity (Stealth) check or an initiative roll, you can expend one superiority die and add the die to the roll, provided you aren't incapacitated."},
  ["optionalfeature.ambush.xphb2024"]={title="Ambush",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 94\n\nWhen you make a Dexterity (XPHB) check or an XPHB roll, you can expend one Superiority Die and add the die to the roll, unless you have the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.ambush-drake.hotdq2014"]={title="Ambush Drake",subtitle="Criatura - HotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 88\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 22 (4d6 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 15 | CON 14 | INT 4 | WIS 11 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Draconic but can't speak it\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe drake has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the drake's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\nSurprise Attack\n\nIf the drake surprises a creature and hits it with an attack during the first round of combat, the target takes an extra 7 (2d6) damage from the attack.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d6 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["feature.ambush-master.xge2024.rogue.scout.13"]={title="Ambush Master",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 47\n\nStarting at 13th level, you excel at leading ambushes and acting first in a fight.\n\nYou have advantage on initiative rolls. In addition, the first creature you hit during the first round of a combat becomes easier for you and others to strike; attack rolls against that target have advantage until the start of your next turn."},
  ["creature.amelia-ghallen.dsotdq2014"]={title="Amelia Ghallen",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 180\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["item.amethyst.dmg2014"]={title="Amethyst",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent deep purple gemstone."},
  ["item.amethyst.xdmg2024"]={title="Amethyst",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA deep purple gemstone."},
  ["creature.amethyst-dragon-wyrmling.ftd2014"]={title="Amethyst Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 162\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 75 (10d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60, swim: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: force, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe both air and water.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) force damage.\n\nSingularity Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon creates a shining bead of gravitational force in its mouth, then releases the energy in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 13 Strength saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 22 (5d8) force damage, and its speed becomes 0 until the start of the dragon's next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage, and its speed isn't reduced."},
  ["creature.amethyst-greatwyrm.ftd2014"]={title="Amethyst Greatwyrm",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 26\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 507 (26d20 + 234)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, burrow: 60, fly: 120, swim: 60\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 14 | CON 29 | INT 30 | WIS 24 | CHA 25\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: force\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nGem Awakening (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIf the greatwyrm would be reduced to 0 hit points, its current hit point total instead resets to 400 hit points, it recharges its Breath Weapon, and it regains any expended uses of Legendary Resistance. Additionally, the greatwyrm can now use its Mass Telekinesis action during the next hour. Award a party an additional 90,000 XP (180,000 XP total) for defeating the greatwyrm after its Gem Awakening activates.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the greatwyrm fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe greatwyrm doesn't require food or drink.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h20 (2d10 + 9) piercing damage plus 16 (3d10) force damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (2d8 + 9) slashing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 19) and is restrained until this grapple ends. The greatwyrm can have only one creature grappled in this way at a time.\n\nBreath Weapon {@recharge 5}\n\nThe greatwyrm exhales crushing force in a 300-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 25 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 71 (11d12) force damage and is knocked prone. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and isn't knocked prone. On a success or failure, the creature's speed becomes 0 until the end of its next turn.\n\nMass Telekinesis (Gem Awakening Only; Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe greatwyrm targets any number of creatures and objects it can see within 120 feet of it. No one target can weigh more than 4,000 pounds, and objects can't be targeted if they're being worn or carried. Each targeted creature must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or be restrained in the greatwyrm's telekinetic grip. At the end of a creature's turn, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nAt the end of the greatwyrm's turn, it can move each creature or object it has in its telekinetic grip up to 60 feet in any direction, but not beyond 120 feet of itself. In addition, it can choose any number of creatures restrained in this way and deal 45 (7d12) force damage to each of them.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe greatwyrm magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the greatwyrm is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe greatwyrm magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nPsychic Beam (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm emits a beam of psychic energy in a 90-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that area must make a 26 Intelligence saving throw, taking 27 (5d10) psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["magicitem.amethyst-lodestone.ftd2014"]={title="Amethyst Lodestone",subtitle="Item Magico - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 22\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis fist-sized chunk of amethyst is infused with an amethyst dragon's ability to bend gravitational forces. While you are carrying the lodestone, you have advantage on Strength saving throws.\n\nThe lodestone has 6 charges for the following properties, which you can use while you are holding the stone. The stone regains 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn.\n\nFlight\n\nAs a bonus action, you can expend 1 charge to gain the power of flight for 10 minutes. For the duration, you gain a flying speed equal to your walking speed, and you can hover.\n\nGravitational Thrust\n\nAs an action, you can expend 1 charge to focus gravity around a creature you can see within 60 feet of you. The target must succeed on a 18 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 20 feet in a direction of your choice.\n\nReverse Gravity\n\nAs an action, you can expend 3 charges to cast reverse gravity from the stone (save 18)."},
  ["creature.ameyali.jttrc2014"]={title="Ameyali",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 108\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.amidor-the-dandelion.wbtw2014"]={title="Amidor the Dandelion",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / S\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 28 (8d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 15 | CON 10 | INT 13 | WIS 12 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpeak with Beasts and Plants\n\nAmidor can communicate with Beasts and Plants as if it shared a language with them.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nRapier\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nSeed Sling\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nAmidor adds 2 to its AC against one melee attack that would hit it. To do so, Amidor must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["creature.ammalia-cassalanter.wdh2014"]={title="Ammalia Cassalanter",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 193\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 45 (10d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 17 | WIS 12 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Elvish, Infernal\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d6 - 1) bludgeoning damage, or 3 (1d8 - 1) bludgeoning damage if used with two hands."},
  ["creature.ammit.psa2014"]={title="Ammit",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.amnizu.mpmm2014"]={title="Amnizu",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 46\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 18\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 202 (27d8 + 81)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 40\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 13 | CON 16 | INT 20 | WIS 12 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal, telepathy 1,000 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the amnizu's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe amnizu has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe amnizu uses Blinding Rot or Forgetfulness, if available. It also makes two Taskmaster Whip attacks.\n\nTaskmaster Whip\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) slashing damage plus 16 (3d10) force damage.\n\nBlinding Rot\n\nThe amnizu targets one or two creatures that it can see within 60 feet of it. Each target must succeed on a 19 Wisdom saving throw or take 26 (4d12) necrotic damage and be blinded until the start of the amnizu's next turn.\n\nForgetfulness {@recharge}\n\nThe amnizu targets one creature it can see within 60 feet of it. That creature must succeed on a 18 Intelligence saving throw or take 26 (4d12) psychic damage and become stunned for 1 minute. A stunned creature repeats the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If the target is stunned for the full minute, it forgets everything it sensed, experienced, and learned during the last 5 hours.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nInstinctive Charm\n\nWhen a creature within 60 feet of the amnizu makes an attack roll against it, and another creature is within the attack's range, the attacker must make a 19 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the attacker must target the creature that is closest to it, not including the amnizu or itself. If multiple creatures are closest, the attacker chooses which one to target. If the saving throw is successful, the attacker is immune to the amnizu's Instinctive Charm for 24 hours."},
  ["creature.amnizu.mtf2014"]={title="Amnizu",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 164\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 18\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 202 (27d8 + 81)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 40\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 13 | CON 16 | INT 20 | WIS 12 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal, telepathy 1,000 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the amnizu's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe amnizu has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe amnizu uses Poison Mind. It also makes two attacks: one with its whip and one with its Disruptive Touch.\n\nTaskmaster Whip\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h10 (2d4 + 5) slashing damage plus 33 (6d10) force damage.\n\nDisruptive Touch\n\nms 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h44 (8d10) necrotic damage.\n\nPoison Mind\n\nThe amnizu targets one or two creatures that it can see within 60 feet of it. Each target must succeed on a 19 Wisdom saving throw or take 26 (4d12) necrotic damage and is blinded until the start of the amnizu's next turn.\n\nForgetfulness {@recharge}\n\nThe amnizu targets one creature it can see within 60 feet of it. That creature must make a 18 Intelligence saving throw and on a failure the target is stunned for 1 minute. A stunned creature repeats the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If the target remains stunned for the full minute, it forgets everything it sensed, experienced, and learned during the last 5 hours.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nInstinctive Charm\n\nWhen a creature within 60 feet of the amnizu makes an attack roll against it, and another creature is within the attack's range, the attacker must make a 19 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the attacker must target the creature that is closest to it, not including the amnizu or itself. If multiple creatures are closest, the attacker chooses which one to target. If the saving throw is successful, the attacker is immune to the amnizu's Instinctive Charm for 24 hours."},
  ["feature.among-the-dead.scag2014.warlock.undying.1"]={title="Among the Dead",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 139\n\nStarting at 1st level, you learn the spare the dying cantrip, which counts as a warlock cantrip for you. You also have advantage on saving throws against any disease.\n\nAdditionally, undead have difficulty harming you. If an undead targets you directly with an attack or a harmful spell, that creature must make a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC (an undead needn't make the save when it includes you in an area effect, such as the explosion of fireball). On a failed save, the creature must choose a new target or forfeit targeting someone instead of you, potentially wasting the attack or spell. On a successful save, the creature is immune to this effect for 24 hours. An undead is also immune to this effect for 24 hours if you target it with an attack or a harmful spell."},
  ["creature.amonkhet-dragon-wyrmling.psa2014"]={title="Amonkhet Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 5"},
  ["creature.amonkhet-hydra.psa2014"]={title="Amonkhet Hydra",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.amonkhet-mummy.psa2014"]={title="Amonkhet Mummy",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.amonkhet-mummy-lord.psa2014"]={title="Amonkhet Mummy Lord",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.amonkhet-sphinx.psa2014"]={title="Amonkhet Sphinx",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.amphisbaena.gos2014"]={title="Amphisbaena",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 230\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 18 | CON 12 | INT 3 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTwo Heads\n\nThe amphisbaena has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks and on saving throws against being blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, stunned, and knocked unconscious.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe amphisbaena makes two bite attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) piercing damage, and the target must make a 11 Constitution saving throw, taking 3 (1d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.amphisbaena.tftyp2014"]={title="Amphisbaena",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 84\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 3"},
  ["creature.amrik-vanthampur.bgdia2014"]={title="Amrik Vanthampur",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 66 (12d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 18 | CON 12 | INT 14 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSuave Defense\n\nWhile Amrik is wearing light or no armor and wielding no shield, his AC includes his Charisma modifier.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAmrik makes three dagger attacks.\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nSmoke Bomb (1/Day)\n\nAmrik hurls a smoke bomb up to 20 feet away. The bomb explodes on impact, creating a cloud of black smoke that fills a 10-foot-radius sphere. The area within the cloud is Vision and Light. A strong wind disperses the cloud, which otherwise remains until the end of Amrik's next turn."},
  ["item.amulet.phb2014"]={title="Amulet",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.amulet.xphb2024"]={title="Amulet",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 226\n\nRaridade: none\n\nFor an Amulet to be an effective Holy Symbol, it must be worn or held."},
  ["magicitem.amulet-of-appearance.coa2014"]={title="Amulet of Appearance",subtitle="Item Magico - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 267\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYour armor, weapons, and other equipment always shine as if just polished. Even if you're wounded, your wounds do not appear to others. You're immune to the frightened and poisoned conditions, as these would otherwise ruin your elegant appearance. However, whenever you would otherwise have been affected by one of these conditions, a random non-evil Humanoid on the Material Plane whom you have previously met gets the condition instead. You know this."},
  ["magicitem.amulet-of-betrayal.coa2014"]={title="Amulet of Betrayal",subtitle="Item Magico - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 267\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou can use a bonus action to move one of the following conditions from yourself to an ally within 60 feet of you: blinded, deafened, frightened, poisoned, stunned, exhaustion. When transferring exhaustion, move all your exhaustion levels. If the chosen ally is immune to a transferred condition, the transfer fails."},
  ["item.amulet-of-dinosaur-feathers-sun-empire.psx2014"]={title="Amulet of dinosaur feathers (Sun Empire)",subtitle="Item - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["magicitem.amulet-of-duplicity.coa2014"]={title="Amulet of Duplicity",subtitle="Item Magico - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 267\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhen you die, you're transported to an extradimensional space where you're stabilized at 0 hit points and kept in that state. The amulet creates a perfect copy of your corpse and places it where you were just before you died, but without any of your worn or carried items. After 24 hours, you regain 1 hit point and are returned to the location of your near-death. Everything about you is the same, except that your facial features are entirely different from before. Only a Wish spell can restore your true identity.\n\nUntil then, you have disadvantage on any Charisma (Persuasion) checks to attempt to reveal who you really are.\n\nCurse\n\nAn Identify spell or similar reveals only that the amulet can prevent death. Once you attune to the amulet, you can't describe its ability to any other creature, and if unattuned, you immediately forget what the amulet does. A Remove Curse spell reveals the details of the curse but does not remove it from the amulet."},
  ["magicitem.amulet-of-harmony.nrh-at2014"]={title="Amulet of Harmony",subtitle="Item Magico - NRH-AT - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThe amulet is a golden disk about 4 inches across. There are symbols etched into its surface and there are six bezels that hold the Gems of Power.\n\nThe Amulet of Harmony has the following properties:\n\n• While attuned to this amulet, you feel a pull in the direction of the Prismatic Well.\n\n• If the Prismatic Well is dormant, you can restore its power by expending your own energy. You must be within 10-feet of the well to restore its power and you must say the words, \"I invoke the power of the Prismatic Well and restore the colors of Harmony for all.\" If you do so, roll a d6. On a 2-6, the power of the well is restored. On a 1, the well is restored but you fall into a deep, magical slumber for 1 year and cannot be roused except by a remove curse spell or similar magic.\n\n• You can turn off the power of the Prismatic Well, plunging all of Harmony into a polarized world where everything is horribly black and white. To do this, you must be within 10-feet of the well and you must say the words, \"I revoke the power of the Prismatic Well and withhold the colors of Harmony to all.\" If you do so, roll a d6. On a 3-6, the well is turned off. On 1-2, the power of the well remains and you turn into a statue of black stone.\n\nOnly a wish spell can undo this effect."},
  ["magicitem.amulet-of-health.dmg2014"]={title="Amulet of Health",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYour Constitution score is 19 while you wear this amulet. It has no effect on you if your Constitution score is already 19 or higher without it."},
  ["magicitem.amulet-of-health.xdmg2024"]={title="Amulet of Health",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 228\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYour Constitution score is 19 while you wear this amulet. It has no effect on you if your Constitution is already 19 or higher without it."},
  ["magicitem.amulet-of-proof-against-detection-and-location.dmg2014"]={title="Amulet of Proof against Detection and Location",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing this amulet, you are hidden from spells magic. You can't be targeted by such magic or perceived through magical scrying sensors."},
  ["magicitem.amulet-of-proof-against-detection-and-location.xdmg2024"]={title="Amulet of Proof against Detection and Location",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 228\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing this amulet, you can't be targeted by Divination spells or perceived through magical scrying sensors unless you allow it."},
  ["magicitem.amulet-of-protection-from-turning.tftyp2014"]={title="Amulet of Protection from Turning",subtitle="Item Magico - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile you wear this amulet of silver and turquoise, you have advantage on saving throws against effects that turn undead.\n\nIf you fail a saving throw against such an effect, you can choose to succeed instead. You can do so three times, and expended uses recharge daily at dawn. Each time an effect that turns undead is used against you, the amulet glows with silvery blue light for a few seconds."},
  ["magicitem.amulet-of-the-black-skull.toa2014"]={title="Amulet of the Black Skull",subtitle="Item Magico - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis amulet is carved from obsidian and shaped like a screaming humanoid skull, with ruby eyes and emeralds for teeth. It hangs from an iron chain necklace.\n\nThe amulet has 6 charges and regains 1d6 charges daily at dawn. While wearing the amulet, you can use an action to expend 1 of its charges to transport yourself and anything you are wearing or carrying to a location within 100 feet of you. The destination you choose doesn't need to be in your line of sight, but it must be familiar to you (in other words, a place you have seen or visited), and it must be on the same plane of existence as you. This effect isn't subject to the magic restrictions placed on the Tomb of the Nine Gods; thus, the amulet can be used to enter and exit the tomb.\n\nIf you aren't undead, you must make a 16 Constitution saving throw each time you use the amulet to teleport. On a failed saving throw, the black skull cackles as you are transformed in transit. The transformation takes effect as soon as you arrive at the destination, and is determined randomly by rolling percentile dice and consulting the Black Skull Transformation table.\n\nd100 | Transformation\n\n01-20 | The symbol of ToA is burned into your flesh, a curse that can only be removed with a remove curse spell or similar magic. Until the curse ends, your hit points can't be restored by magic.\n\n21-35 | You grow larger as if affected by an enlarge/reduce spell, except the effect lasts for 1 hour.\n\n36-50 | You grow smaller as if affected by an enlarge/reduce spell, except the effect lasts for 1 hour.\n\n51-70 | You arrive at the destination wearing nothing but the amulet of the black skull. Everything else that you were wearing or carrying appears in a random unoccupied space within 100 feet of you.\n\n71-95 | You are paralyzed for 1 minute or until this effect is ended with a lesser restoration spell or similar magic.\n\n96-00 | You become petrified. This effect can be ended only with a greater restoration spell or similar magic."},
  ["magicitem.amulet-of-the-drunkard.egw2014"]={title="Amulet of the Drunkard",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 265\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis amulet smells of old, ale-stained wood. While wearing it, you can regain 4d4 + 4 hit points when you drink a pint of beer, ale, mead, or wine. Once the amulet has restored hit points, it can't do so again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.amulet-of-the-inferno.coa2014"]={title="Amulet of the Inferno",subtitle="Item Magico - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 273\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nWhen Fierna was born, petitioners and devils from all over came to celebrate her birth. Many brought gifts and treasures, including a powerful infernal warlock. Recognizing the strength and inner fire of Fierna, the warlock gifted her with the Amulet of the Inferno, and it has been around her neck ever since.\n\nThe Amulet of the Inferno is a magic necklace that grants a +3 bonus to spell save DC and spell attack bonus.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nThe Amulet of the Inferno has the following random properties:\n\n• 3 dmg properties\n\n• 2 dmg properties\n\nInfernal Fire\n\nWhile worn, the amulet augments any magical flames created by you, transforming normal fire into Hellfire. Hellfire ignores resistances and immunities to fire damage and deals double damage to creatures vulnerable to either fire or necrotic damage. It is also capable of melting stone, as well as igniting flammable objects.\n\nRaging Inferno\n\nWhile attuned to the Amulet of the Inferno, you may use a bonus action to cast Fire Bolt or Produce Flame. The cantrips scale based on your total character level and use Intelligence as a spellcasting modifier if you're normally incapable of casting spells.\n\nEverburning\n\nThe Amulet of the Inferno grants resistance to cold damage and the ability to breathe underwater. Any magical flames you conjure are similarly augmented: they can be used underwater, can't be extinguished through any means, and can exude any temperature. While the casting of a fire spell can still be interrupted with Counterspell, once the spell has been cast, any lingering flames can't be removed.\n\nDestroying the Amulet\n\nThe only creature capable of destroying the amulet is the warlock that created it. Nobody living knows the warlock's identity, making destroying the amulet almost impossible."},
  ["magicitem.amulet-of-the-planes.dmg2014"]={title="Amulet of the Planes",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile wearing this amulet, you can use an action to name a location that you are familiar with on another plane of existence. Then make a 15 Intelligence check. On a successful check, you cast the plane shift spell. On a failure, you and each creature and object within 15 feet of you travel to a random destination. Roll a d100. On a 1-60, you travel to a random location on the plane you named. On a 61-100, you travel to a randomly determined plane of existence."},
  ["magicitem.amulet-of-the-planes.xdmg2024"]={title="Amulet of the Planes",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 229\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile wearing this amulet, you can take a XPHB action to name a location that you are familiar with on another plane of existence. Then make a 15 Intelligence (XPHB) check. On a successful check, you cast XPHB. On a failed check, you and each creature and object within 15 feet of you travel to a random destination determined by rolling 1d100 and consulting the following table.\n\n1d100 | Destination\n\n01-60 | Random location on the plane you named\n\n61-70 | Random location on an Inner Plane determined by rolling 1d6: on a 1, the Plane of Air; on a 2, the Plane of Earth; on a 3, the Plane of Fire; on a 4, the Plane of Water; on a 5, the Feywild; on a 6, the Shadowfell\n\n71-80 | Random location on an Outer Plane determined by rolling 1d8: on a 1, Arborea; on a 2, Arcadia; on a 3, the Beastlands; on a 4, Bytopia; on a 5, Elysium; on a 6, Mechanus; on a 7, Mount Celestia; on an 8, Ysgard\n\n81-90 | Random location on an Outer Plane determined by rolling 1d8: on a 1, the Abyss; on a 2, Acheron; on a 3, Carceri; on a 4, Gehenna; on a 5, Hades; on a 6, Limbo; on a 7, the Nine Hells; on an 8, Pandemonium\n\n91-00 | Random location on the Astral Plane"},
  ["creature.amun-sa.qftis2014"]={title="Amun Sa",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 106\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.anacreda.coa2014"]={title="Anacreda",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 146\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / L\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 253 (22d10 + 132)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 40\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 16 | CON 22 | INT 15 | WIS 16 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft., truesight 10 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant, Infernal, Sylvan\n\nImunidades: cold, fire\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAnacreda makes two Claw attacks. She can replace one of the attacks with a Crushing Hug attack.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (2d8 + 7) slashing damage.\n\nCrushing Hug\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h51 (8d10 + 7) bludgeoning damage, and if the target is a Large or smaller creature, Anacreda grabs it with both arms. The target has the grappled condition (escape 18). Until the grapple ends, the target takes 73 (12d10 + 7) necrotic damage at the start of each of Anacreda's turns. Anacreda can't make attacks while grappling a creature in this way.\n\nSpinewall\n\nAnacreda causes a 50-foot-long, 5-foot-wide row of bones to pierce the earth at a point within 120 feet of her. She chooses the direction of the line. The bones rise 10 feet into the air and form a solid wall. A 5-foot section of bone has an AC of 20 and 10 hit points.\n\nShattering Shriek (1/Day)\n\nAnacreda shrieks loud enough to shatter stone and bone alike. Each creature within a 50-foot-radius sphere centered on Anacreda must make a 18 Constitution saving throw. A creature takes 55 (10d10) thunder damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Unworked stone, exposed bone, and similar materials in the radius are shattered and turned into difficult terrain."},
  ["creature.anagwendol.coa2014"]={title="Anagwendol",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 262\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / M\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 190 (20d8 + 100)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 90\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 18 | CON 20 | INT 18 | WIS 20 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nAnagwendol has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAnagwendol makes two attacks using her Defending Greatsword, Longbow, or a combination of the two.\n\nDefending Greatsword\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h19 (4d6 + 5) slashing damage plus 22 (5d8) radiant damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 9 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage damage plus 22 (5d8) radiant damage.\n\nHealing Touch (2/Day)\n\nAnagwendol touches another creature. The target magically regains 30 (6d8 + 3) hit points and is freed from any curse, disease, poison, blindness, or deafness.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nDefensive Sword-work\n\nAnagwendol can forgo attacking with her Defending Greatsword on this turn and gain a +3 to her armor class. She can still attack with her Longbow."},
  ["creature.anarch.ggr2014"]={title="Anarch",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 239\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 13 | CON 12 | INT 9 | WIS 11 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAggressive\n\nAs a bonus action, the anarch can move up to its speed toward a hostile creature it can see.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe anarch deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSpiked Club\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage, or 7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage if used with two hands."},
  ["creature.anastrasya-karelova.cos2014"]={title="Anastrasya Karelova",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 93\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["feature.ancestral-protectors.xge2024.barbarian.ancestral-guardian.3"]={title="Ancestral Protectors",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 9\n\nStarting when you choose this path at 3rd level, spectral warriors appear when you enter your rage. While you're raging, the first creature you hit with an attack on your turn becomes the target of the warriors, which hinder its attacks. Until the start of your next turn, that target has disadvantage on any attack roll that isn't against you, and when the target hits a creature other than you with an attack, that creature has resistance to the damage dealt by the attack. The effect on the target ends early if your rage ends."},
  ["creature.anchorite-of-talos.dip2014"]={title="Anchorite of Talos",subtitle="Criatura - DIP - 2014",body="Pagina: 51\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 58 (9d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 9 | WIS 15 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Orc\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShapechanger\n\nThe anchorite can use its action to polymorph into a boar or back into its true form, which is humanoid. Its statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClawed Gauntlet (Humanoid Form Only)\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nTusk (Boar Form Only)\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.ancient-amethyst-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Ancient Amethyst Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 160\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 444 (24d20 + 192)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 26 | DEX 14 | CON 27 | INT 26 | WIS 19 | CHA 23\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: force, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe both air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h19 (2d10 + 8) piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) force damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d6 + 8) slashing damage.\n\nSingularity Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon creates a shining bead of gravitational force in its mouth, then releases the energy in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 23 Strength saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 63 (14d8) force damage, and its speed becomes 0 until the start of the dragon's next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage, and its speed isn't reduced.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe dragon magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe dragon makes one claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nExplosive Crystal (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe dragon spits an amethyst that explodes at a point it can see within 60 feet of it. Each creature within a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must succeed on a 23 Dexterity saving throw or take 18 (4d8) force damage and be knocked prone."},
  ["creature.ancient-amonkhet-dragon.psa2014"]={title="Ancient Amonkhet Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 10"},
  ["creature.ancient-black-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Ancient Black Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 87\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 367 (21d20 + 147)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 14 | CON 25 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h19 (2d10 + 8) piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) acid damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d6 + 8) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h17 (2d8 + 8) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 19 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nAcid Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales acid in a 90-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 22 Dexterity saving throw, taking 67 (15d8) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 15 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 23 Dexterity saving throw or take 15 (2d6 + 8) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.ancient-black-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Ancient Black Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 40\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 367 (21d20 + 147)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 14 | CON 25 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 4 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 15, reach 15 ft. h17 (2d8 + 8) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Acid damage.\n\nAcid Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 22, each creature in a 90-foot-long, 10-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 67 (15d8) Acid damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCloud of Insects\n\ndex 21, one creature the dragon can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 33 (6d10) Poison damage, and the target has XPHB on saving throws to maintain XPHB until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB. The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.ancient-blue-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Ancient Blue Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 90\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 481 (26d20 + 208)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 29 | DEX 10 | CON 27 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h20 (2d10 + 9) piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) lightning damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d6 + 9) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h18 (2d8 + 9) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 20 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales lightning in a 120-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 23 Dexterity saving throw, taking 88 (16d10) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 15 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 24 Dexterity saving throw or take 16 (2d6 + 9) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.ancient-blue-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Ancient Blue Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 50\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 481 (26d20 + 208)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 29 | DEX 10 | CON 27 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 25\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 3 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 16, reach 15 ft. h18 (2d8 + 9) Slashing damage plus 11 (2d10) Lightning damage.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 23, each creature in a 120-foot-long, 10-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 88 (16d10) Lightning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCloaked Flight\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB on itself, and it can fly up to half its XPHB. The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nSonic Boom\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 3 version). The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nTail Swipe\n\nThe dragon makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.ancient-brass-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Ancient Brass Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 104\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 20\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 297 (17d20 + 119)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 10 | CON 25 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h19 (2d10 + 8) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d6 + 8) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h17 (2d8 + 8) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 18 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons:\n\n• Fire Breath\n\n• Sleep Breath\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically polymorphs into a humanoid or beast that has a challenge rating no higher than its own, or back into its true form. It reverts to its true form if it dies. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying is absorbed or borne by the new form (the dragon's choice).\n\nIn a new form, the dragon retains its alignment, hit points, Hit Dice, ability to speak, proficiencies, Legendary Resistance, lair actions, and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores, as well as this action. Its statistics and capabilities are otherwise replaced by those of the new form, except any class features or legendary actions of that form.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 15 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 22 Dexterity saving throw or take 15 (2d6 + 8) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.ancient-brass-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Ancient Brass Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 56\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 20\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 332 (19d20 + 133)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 10 | CON 25 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of (A) Sleep Breath or (B) Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 3 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 14, reach 15 ft. h19 (2d10 + 8) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Fire damage.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 21, each creature in a 90-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 58 (13d8) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nSleep Breath\n\ncon 21, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn, at which point it repeats the save. 2 The target has the XPHB condition for 10 minutes. This effect ends for the target if it takes damage or a creature within 5 feet of it takes an action to wake it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nBlazing Light\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 3 version).\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack.\n\nScorching Sands\n\ndex 20, one creature the dragon can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 36 (8d8) Fire damage, and the target's XPHB is halved until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn."},
  ["creature.ancient-bronze-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Ancient Bronze Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 107\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 444 (24d20 + 192)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 29 | DEX 10 | CON 27 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h20 (2d10 + 9) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d6 + 9) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h18 (2d8 + 9) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 20 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Lightning Breath\n\n• Repulsion Breath\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically polymorphs into a humanoid or beast that has a challenge rating no higher than its own, or back into its true form. It reverts to its true form if it dies. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying is absorbed or borne by the new form (the dragon's choice).\n\nIn a new form, the dragon retains its alignment, hit points, Hit Dice, ability to speak, proficiencies, Legendary Resistance, lair actions, and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores, as well as this action. Its statistics and capabilities are otherwise replaced by those of the new form, except any class features or legendary actions of that form.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 15 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 24 Dexterity saving throw or take 16 (2d6 + 9) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.ancient-bronze-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Ancient Bronze Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 60\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 444 (24d20 + 192)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 29 | DEX 10 | CON 27 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 25\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of (A) Repulsion Breath or (B) Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 16, reach 15 ft. h18 (2d8 + 9) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Lightning damage.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 23, each creature in a 120-foot-long, 10-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 82 (15d10) Lightning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nRepulsion Breath\n\nstr 23, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target is pushed up to 60 feet straight away from the dragon and has the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nGuiding Light\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version).\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack.\n\nThunderclap\n\ncon 22, each creature in a 20-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point the dragon can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 13 (3d8) Thunder damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.ancient-copper-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Ancient Copper Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 110\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 350 (20d20 + 140)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 12 | CON 25 | INT 20 | WIS 17 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h19 (2d10 + 8) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d6 + 8) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h17 (2d8 + 8) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 19 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Acid Breath\n\n• Slowing Breath\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically polymorphs into a humanoid or beast that has a challenge rating no higher than its own, or back into its true form. It reverts to its true form if it dies. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying is absorbed or borne by the new form (the dragon's choice).\n\nIn a new form, the dragon retains its alignment, hit points, Hit Dice, ability to speak, proficiencies, Legendary Resistance, lair actions, and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores, as well as this action. Its statistics and capabilities are otherwise replaced by those of the new form, except any class features or legendary actions of that form.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 15 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 23 Dexterity saving throw or take 15 (2d6 + 8) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.ancient-copper-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Ancient Copper Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 80\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 367 (21d20 + 147)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 12 | CON 25 | INT 20 | WIS 17 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of (A) Slowing Breath or (B) Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 5 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 15, reach 15 ft. h19 (2d10 + 8) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Acid damage.\n\nAcid Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 22, each creature in an 90-foot-long, 10-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 63 (14d8) Acid damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nSlowing Breath\n\ncon 22, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target can't take Reactions; its XPHB is halved; and it can take either an action or a XPHB on its turn, not both. This effect lasts until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nGiggling Magic\n\ncha 21, one creature the dragon can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 31 (9d6) Psychic damage. Until the end of its next turn, the target rolls 1d8 whenever it makes an ability check or attack roll and subtracts the number rolled from the XPHB. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nMind Jolt\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 5 version). The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.ancient-crystal-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Ancient Crystal Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 170\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 19\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 222 (12d20 + 96)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 12 | CON 26 | INT 20 | WIS 16 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, radiant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h18 (2d10 + 7) piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) radiant damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h14 (2d6 + 7) slashing damage.\n\nScintillating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a burst of brilliant radiance in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 22 Constitution saving throw, taking 49 (11d8) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The dragon then gains 25 temporary hit points by absorbing a portion of the radiant energy.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe dragon magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe dragon makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nStarlight Strike (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe dragon releases a searing beam of starlight at a creature that it can see within 60 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 19 Dexterity saving throw or take 38 (11d6) radiant damage."},
  ["creature.ancient-deep-crow.ai2014"]={title="Ancient Deep Crow",subtitle="Criatura - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 187 (15d12 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 16 | CON 23 | INT 10 | WIS 15 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Crow\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe ancient deep crow has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nShadow Stealth\n\nWhile in dim light or darkness, the ancient deep crow can take the Hide action as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe ancient deep crow makes three attacks: one with its mandibles and two with its claws.\n\nMandibles\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage, and the target is grappled (escape 19). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the ancient deep crow can't use its mandibles on another target.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nShadow Caw\n\nThe ancient deep crow releases an ear-splitting caw. Each creature within 60 feet of the crow and able to hear it must make a 17 Constitution saving throw. On a failure, a creature takes 10 (3d6) psychic damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe deep crow makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nShadow Caw (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe ancient deep crow uses Shadow Caw.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe ancient deep crow beats its wings. Each creature within 10 feet of the deep crow must succeed on a 19 Dexterity saving throw or take 13 (2d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The ancient deep crow can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.ancient-deep-dragon.fraif2014"]={title="Ancient Deep Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 259\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 18\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 247 (15d20 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 16 | CON 22 | INT 19 | WIS 18 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 300 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Undercommon\n\nResistencias: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 12, reach 15 ft. h17 (2d10 + 6) Slashing damage plus 5 (1d10) Poison damage.\n\nNightmare Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nwis 20, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 44 (8d10) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of the dragon's next turn. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShape-Shift\n\nThe dragon shape-shifts into a Small or Medium Humanoid or a Small or Medium Beast, or it returns to its true form. Its game statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack.\n\nSpore Salvo\n\ncon 20, one creature within 30 feet of the dragon that it can see. actSaveFail 16 (3d10) Poison damage, and the target has the XPHB condition. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn."},
  ["creature.ancient-deep-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Ancient Deep Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 173\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 18\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 201 (13d20 + 65)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 16 | CON 20 | INT 19 | WIS 18 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 300 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Undercommon\n\nResistencias: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) poison damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h10 (1d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 20 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses its action to end it.\n\nNightmare Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a cloud of spores in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 19 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 49 (9d10) psychic damage, and it is frightened of the dragon for 1 minute. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage with no additional effects. A frightened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCommanding Spores\n\nThe dragon releases spores around a creature within 30 feet of it that it can see. The target must succeed on a 19 Wisdom saving throw or use its reaction to make a melee weapon attack against a random creature within reach. If no creatures are within reach, or the target can't take a reaction, it takes 11 (2d10) psychic damage.\n\nTail\n\nThe dragon makes one Tail attack.\n\nSpore Salvo (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon releases poisonous spores around a creature within 30 feet of it that it can see. The target must succeed on a 19 Constitution saving throw or take 28 (8d6) poison damage and become poisoned for 1 minute. The poisoned creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.ancient-dragon-turtle.ftd2014"]={title="Ancient Dragon Turtle",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 191\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 24\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 409 (21d20 + 189)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 60\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 12 | CON 29 | INT 14 | WIS 19 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Aquan, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold, fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon turtle can breathe air and water.\n\nBlessing of the Sea (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIf the dragon turtle would be reduced to 0 hit points, its current hit point total instead resets to 350 hit points, and it recharges its Steam Breath. Additionally, the dragon turtle can now use the options in the \"Mythic Actions\" section for 1 hour. Award a party an additional 62,000 XP (124,000 XP total) for defeating the dragon turtle after its Blessing of the Sea activates.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon turtle fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe dragon turtle doesn't require food or drink.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon turtle makes one Bite or Tail attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h15 (1d12 + 9) piercing damage plus 13 (2d12) lightning damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h18 (2d8 + 9) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h20 (2d10 + 9) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 24 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nSteam Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon turtle exhales steam in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 24 Constitution saving throw, taking 67 (15d8) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Being underwater doesn't grant resistance against this damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nThe dragon turtle makes one Claw or Tail attack.\n\nMove\n\nThe dragon turtle moves up to its speed. If the dragon turtle is swimming, this movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks.\n\nBoiling Aura (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe dragon turtle radiates intense heat. Until the start of the dragon turtle's next turn, whenever a creature starts its turn within 20 feet of the dragon turtle, that creature must succeed on a 24 Constitution saving throw or take 40 (9d8) fire damage. Being underwater doesn't grant resistance against this damage.\n\n=== ACOES MITICAS ===\n\nBite\n\nThe dragon turtle makes one Bite attack.\n\nArmor of Storms (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nLightning temporarily surrounds the dragon turtle, and it gains 40 temporary hit points until the start of its next turn. Until all these temporary hit points are gone, any creature that touches the dragon turtle or hits it with a melee attack takes 26 (4d12) lightning damage."},
  ["creature.ancient-emerald-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Ancient Emerald Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 195\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 332 (19d20 + 133)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 12 | CON 25 | INT 20 | WIS 18 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: fire, psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and can leave a 20-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\nWarp Perception (1/Day)\n\nThe dragon can cast mirage arcane, requiring no spell components and using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h18 (2d10 + 7) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) psychic damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h14 (2d6 + 7) slashing damage.\n\nDisorienting Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a wave of psychic dissonance in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 22 Intelligence saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 56 (16d6) psychic damage, and until the end of its next turn, when the creature makes an attack roll or an ability check, it must roll a d8 and reduce the total by the number rolled. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage with no additional effects.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe dragon magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe dragon makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nEmerald Embers (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe dragon creates a dancing mote of green flame around a creature it can see within 60 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 20 Dexterity saving throw or take 42 (12d6) fire damage."},
  ["creature.ancient-gold-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Ancient Gold Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 113\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 24\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 546 (28d20 + 252)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 14 | CON 29 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 28\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h21 (2d10 + 10) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d6 + 10) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h19 (2d8 + 10) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 24 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Fire Breath\n\n• Weakening Breath\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically polymorphs into a humanoid or beast that has a challenge rating no higher than its own, or back into its true form. It reverts to its true form if it dies. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying is absorbed or borne by the new form (the dragon's choice).\n\nIn a new form, the dragon retains its alignment, hit points, Hit Dice, ability to speak, proficiencies, Legendary Resistance, lair actions, and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores, as well as this action. Its statistics and capabilities are otherwise replaced by those of the new form, except any class features or legendary actions of that form.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 15 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 25 Dexterity saving throw or take 17 (2d6 + 10) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.ancient-gold-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Ancient Gold Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 146\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 24\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 546 (28d20 + 252)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 14 | CON 29 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 28\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of (A) Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 4 version) or (B) Weakening Breath.\n\nRend\n\nm 17 to hit, reach 15 ft. h19 (2d8 + 10) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Fire damage.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 24, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 71 (13d10) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nWeakening Breath\n\nstr 24, each creature that isn't currently affected by this breath in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target has XPHB on Strength-based XPHB and subtracts 5 (1d10) from its damage rolls. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nBanish\n\ncha 24, one creature the dragon can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 24 (7d6) Force damage, and the target has the XPHB condition and is transported to a harmless demiplane until the start of the dragon's next turn, at which point it reappears in an unoccupied space of the dragon's choice within 120 feet of the dragon. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nGuiding Light\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 4 version).\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.ancient-green-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Ancient Green Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 93\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 385 (22d20 + 154)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 12 | CON 25 | INT 20 | WIS 17 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h19 (2d10 + 8) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) poison damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h22 (4d6 + 8) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h17 (2d8 + 8) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 19 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nPoison Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales poisonous gas in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 22 Constitution saving throw, taking 77 (22d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 15 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 23 Dexterity saving throw or take 15 (2d6 + 8) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.ancient-green-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Ancient Green Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 154\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 402 (23d20 + 161)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 12 | CON 25 | INT 20 | WIS 17 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 5 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 15, reach 15 ft. h17 (2d8 + 8) Slashing damage plus 10 (3d6) Poison damage.\n\nPoison Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 22, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 77 (22d6) Poison damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nMind Invasion\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 5 version).\n\nNoxious Miasma\n\ncon 21, each creature in a 30-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point the dragon can see within 90 feet. actSaveFail 17 (5d6) Poison damage, and the target takes a -2 penalty to AC until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.ancient-lunar-dragon.bam2014"]={title="Ancient Lunar Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 19\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 297 (17d20 + 119)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 20, fly: 80\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 12 | CON 24 | INT 12 | WIS 15 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 240 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and leaves a 20-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe dragon doesn't require air.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h15 (2d6 + 8) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) cold damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d6 + 8) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h15 (2d6 + 8) bludgeoning damage.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a blast of frost in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in the cone must make a 21 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 36 (8d8) cold damage, and its speed is reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage, and its speed isn't reduced.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nPhase (3/Day)\n\nThe dragon becomes partially incorporeal for as long as it maintains concentration on the effect (as if concentration on a spell). While partially incorporeal, the dragon has resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes one Tail attack.\n\nTreacherous Ice\n\nMagical ice covers the ground in a 20-foot radius centered on a point the dragon can see within 120 feet of itself. The ice, which is difficult terrain for all creatures except lunar dragons, lasts for 10 minutes or until the dragon uses this legendary action again.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 15 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 21 Dexterity saving throw or take 12 (1d8 + 8) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its speed without provoking opportunity attacks."},
  ["feature.ancient-might.rhw2014.ranger.hollow-warden.15"]={title="Ancient Might",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.ancient-moonstone-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Ancient Moonstone Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 330 (20d20 + 120)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 18 | CON 23 | INT 20 | WIS 22 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) radiant damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h10 (1d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 21 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nBreath Weapon {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons:\n\n• Dream Breath The dragon exhales mist in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 21 Constitution saving throw or fall unconscious for 10 minutes. This effect ends for a creature if the creature takes damage or someone uses an action to wake it.\n\n• Moonlight Breath The dragon exhales a beam of moonlight in a 120-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that area must make a 21 Dexterity saving throw, taking 60 (11d10) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTail\n\nThe dragon makes one Tail attack.\n\nCast a Spell (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting."},
