geoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.ancient-red-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Ancient Red Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 256\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 24\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 507 (26d20 + 234)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 10 | CON 29 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 27\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 3 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 17, reach 15 ft. h19 (2d8 + 10) Slashing damage plus 10 (3d6) Fire damage.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 24, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 91 (26d6) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCommanding Presence\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version). The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nFiery Rays\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 3 version). The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.ancient-sapphire-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Ancient Sapphire Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 370 (20d20 + 160)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 14 | CON 27 | INT 21 | WIS 19 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe dragon can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and can leave a 20-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h19 (2d10 + 8) piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) thunder damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d6 + 8) slashing damage.\n\nDebilitating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a pulse of high-pitched, nearly inaudible sound in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 23 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 55 (10d10) thunder damage and is incapacitated until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe dragon magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe dragon makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nTelekinetic Fling (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe dragon chooses one Medium or smaller object that isn't being worn or carried that it can see within 60 feet of it, and it magically hurls the object at a creature it can see within 60 feet of the object. The target must succeed on a 20 Dexterity saving throw or take 42 (12d6) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.ancient-sea-serpent.ftd2014"]={title="Ancient Sea Serpent",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 170 (11d20 + 55)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 60\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 15 | CON 20 | INT 13 | WIS 16 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe sea serpent can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf the sea serpent fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe sea serpent deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sea serpent makes one Bite attack and one Constrict or Tail attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h20 (2d12 + 7) piercing damage plus 6 (1d12) cold damage.\n\nConstrict\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 20 ft., one creature. h29 (4d10 + 7) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 20). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the sea serpent can't constrict another target.\n\nTail\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h13 (1d12 + 7) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 20 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 30 feet away from the sea serpent and knocked prone.\n\nRime Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe sea serpent exhales a 60-foot cone of cold. Each creature in that area must make a 18 Constitution saving throw, taking 49 (9d10) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTail\n\nThe sea serpent makes one Tail attack.\n\nBite (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe sea serpent makes one Bite attack"},
  ["reward.ancient-seal.vrgr2014"]={title="Ancient Seal",subtitle="Recompensa - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 193\n\nThis curse protects the resting place of a long-dead ruler and punishes any who disturb the ruler's remains or plunder the treasures.\n\nPronouncement\n\nCarved into the stone of the crypt door are the words \"Relentless death follows those who disturb the sovereign's rest.\"\n\nBurden\n\nEach character that gains the curse is hunted by a wraith that appears at sunset and vanishes at dawn, pursuing the single-minded goal of slaying the cursed individual. The wraith manifests in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of its victim. Destroying the wraith grants a temporary reprieve; it doesn't reform for 10 days. You can scale this curse for lower- and higher-level characters by choosing another kind of creature.\n\nResolution\n\nThe cursed character sets right what they disturbed; stolen treasure must be returned, and if the ruler's body was disturbed, it must be reinterred with proper observances."},
  ["creature.ancient-silver-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Ancient Silver Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 487 (25d20 + 225)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 10 | CON 29 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 23\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h21 (2d10 + 10) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d6 + 10) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h19 (2d8 + 10) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 21 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Cold Breath\n\n• Paralyzing Breath\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically polymorphs into a humanoid or beast that has a challenge rating no higher than its own, or back into its true form. It reverts to its true form if it dies. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying is absorbed or borne by the new form (the dragon's choice).\n\nIn a new form, the dragon retains its alignment, hit points, Hit Dice, ability to speak, proficiencies, Legendary Resistance, lair actions, and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores, as well as this action. Its statistics and capabilities are otherwise replaced by those of the new form, except any class features or legendary actions of that form.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 15 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 25 Dexterity saving throw or take 17 (2d6 + 10) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.ancient-silver-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Ancient Silver Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 280\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 468 (24d20 + 216)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 10 | CON 29 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of (A) Paralyzing Breath or (B) Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 17, reach 15 ft. h19 (2d8 + 10) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Cold damage.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 24, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 67 (15d8) Cold damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nParalyzing Breath\n\ncon 24, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. 1 The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn, when it repeats the save. 2 The target has the XPHB condition, and it repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nChill\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB. The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nCold Gale\n\ndex 23, each creature in a 60-foot-long, 10-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Cold damage, and the target is pushed up to 30 feet straight away from the dragon. actSaveSuccess Half damage only. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.ancient-solar-dragon.bam2014"]={title="Ancient Solar Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 425 (23d20 + 184)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 120\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 15 | CON 26 | INT 17 | WIS 18 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 240 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe dragon doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nNebulous Thoughts\n\nMagical attempts to read the dragon's mind or glean its thoughts fail automatically.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe dragon deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe dragon doesn't require air.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and one Tail attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h19 (3d6 + 9) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) radiant damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h13 (1d8 + 9) bludgeoning damage.\n\nPhotonic Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a flashing mote of radiant energy that travels to a point the dragon can see within 240 feet of itself, then blossoms into a 40-foot-radius sphere centered on that point. Each creature in the sphere must make a 23 Constitution saving throw, taking 66 (12d10) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes one Tail attack.\n\nBlinding Brilliance (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon emits magical light in a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on itself. Each creature in this area must succeed on a 23 Wisdom saving throw or be blinded until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.ancient-spirit-dragon.fraif2014"]={title="Ancient Spirit Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 279\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 420 (24d20 + 168)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 26 | DEX 14 | CON 25 | INT 24 | WIS 18 | CHA 23\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of (A) Time-Warping Breath or (B) Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 15, reach 15 ft. h19 (2d10 + 8) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Necrotic damage.\n\nRuinous Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 22, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 72 (16d8) Necrotic damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nTime-Warping Breath\n\nwis 22, each creature that isn't currently affected by this breath in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target's XPHB is halved, it can't take Reactions, and it can take either an action or a XPHB on its turn, not both. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack.\n\nShattering Wave\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version).\n\nUnearth Ruins\n\nThe dragon magically raises broken, ancient ruins in a 20-foot-radius, 60-foot-high XPHB centered on a point it can see within 120 feet. Ground in the XPHB becomes XPHB. Each creature in the XPHB when it appears is subjected to the following effect. str 22. actSaveFail 13 (3d8) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the XPHB condition. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn."},
  ["creature.ancient-time-dragon.mpp2014"]={title="Ancient Time Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 48\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 26\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 536 (29d20 + 232)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 14 | CON 26 | INT 27 | WIS 18 | CHA 23\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCycle of Rebirth\n\nIf the dragon dies, its soul coalesces into a steely egg and teleports to a random plane of existence. The egg is immune to all damage and hatches into a time dragon wyrmling after 1d100 years. The dragon retains all memories and knowledge it gained in its previous life.\n\nLegendary Resistance (5/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h22 (3d8 + 9) slashing damage plus 10 (3d6) force damage.\n\nTime Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a wave of shimmering light in a 90-foot cone. Nonmagical objects and vegetation in that area that aren't being worn or carried crumble to dust. Each creature in that area must make a 24 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 52 (8d12) force damage and is magically weakened as it is desynchronized from the time stream. While the creature is in this state, attack rolls against it have advantage, it has the poisoned condition, and other creatures have resistance to all damage it deals. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage only. A weakened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself after it succeeds on three of these saves.\n\nTime Gate (1/Day)\n\nThe dragon conjures a 20-foot-diameter, circular portal in the space between its horns or in an unoccupied space it can see within 30 feet of itself. The portal links to a precise location on any plane of existence at a point in time up to 8,000 years from the present, whether past or future. The portal lasts for 24 hours or until the dragon's concentration ends (as if concentration on a spell). The portal has a front and a back on each plane where it appears. Travel through the portal is possible only by moving through its front. Anything that does so is transported to the destination, appearing in the unoccupied space nearest to the portal. Deities and other planar rulers can prevent portals created by the dragon from opening in the rulers' presence or anywhere within their domains.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nReactive Rend\n\nAfter using Legendary Resistance or in response to being hit by an attack roll, the dragon makes one Rend attack.\n\nSlow Time\n\nImmediately after a creature the dragon can see ends its turn, the dragon targets a creature it can see within 90 feet of itself that is weakened by its Time Breath. Until the weakened effect ends on the target, its speed becomes 0, and its speed can't increase.\n\nTime Slip\n\nThe dragon halves the damage it takes from an attack made against it, provided it can see the attacker. The dragon can then immediately teleport, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["creature.ancient-topaz-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Ancient Topaz Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 220\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 20\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 280 (17d20 + 102)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 12 | CON 23 | INT 20 | WIS 19 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe both air and water.\n\nFabricate (1/Day)\n\nThe dragon can cast fabricate, requiring no spell components and using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) necrotic damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nDesiccating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales yellowish necrotic energy in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 20 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 49 (14d6) necrotic damage and is weakened until the end of its next turn. A weakened creature has disadvantage on Strength-based ability checks and Strength saving throws, and the creature's weapon attacks that rely on Strength deal half damage. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't weakened.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe dragon magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe dragon makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nEssential Reduction (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe dragon targets a creature or an object not being worn or carried that it can see within 60 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 19 Constitution saving throw or take 40 (9d8) necrotic damage. If this damage reduces the target to 0 hit points, it crumbles to dust."},
  ["creature.ancient-white-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Ancient White Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 100\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 20\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 333 (18d20 + 144)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 26 | DEX 10 | CON 26 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIce Walk\n\nThe dragon can move across and climb icy surfaces without needing to make an ability check. Additionally, difficult terrain composed of ice or snow doesn't cost it extra movement.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h19 (2d10 + 8) piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) cold damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d6 + 8) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h17 (2d8 + 8) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales an icy blast in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 22 Constitution saving throw, taking 72 (16d8) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 15 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 22 Dexterity saving throw or take 15 (2d6 + 8) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.ancient-white-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Ancient White Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 330\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 20\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 333 (18d20 + 144)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 26 | DEX 10 | CON 26 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIce Walk\n\nThe dragon can move across and climb icy surfaces without needing to make an ability check. Additionally, XPHB composed of ice or snow doesn't cost it extra movement.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nFrightful Presence\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 14, reach 15 ft. h17 (2d8 + 8) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Cold damage.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 22, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 63 (14d8) Cold damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nFreezing Burst\n\ncon 20, each creature in a 30-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point the dragon can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Cold damage, and the target's XPHB is 0 until the end of the target's next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.andir-valmakos.dsotdq2014"]={title="Andir Valmakos",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 14 | WIS 11 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBonus Proficiencies\n\nAndir is proficient with simple weapons and light armor.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nArcane Burst\n\nms,rs 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) force damage.\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage, or 4 (1d8) bludgeoning damage if used with two hands."},
  ["creature.andras.imr2014"]={title="Andras",subtitle="Criatura - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant Owl"},
  ["creature.android.qftis2014"]={title="Android",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 194\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 91 (14d8 + 28)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 18 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (sentry only), darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus the languages spoken by its creator\n\nResistencias: acid, fire\n\nImunidades: cold, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDesign Specialization\n\nWhen the android is created, it gains one of six possible designs suited for its role (choose or roll a d6): 1, aerialist; 2, diplomat; 3, diver; 4, duelist; 5, medic; 6, sentry. This design determines certain traits in this stat block.\n\nLightning Overload\n\nWhen the android takes lightning damage, it must succeed on a 10 Constitution saving throw or have the stunned condition until the start of its next turn.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Diplomat and Medic Only)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe android makes two Force Strike attacks.\n\nForce Strike\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 40/120 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) force damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry (Duelist Only)\n\nThe android adds 3 to its AC against one melee attack roll that would hit it. To do so, the android must see the attacker."},
  ["creature.androsphinx.mm2014"]={title="Androsphinx",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 281\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 199 (19d10 + 95)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 60\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 10 | CON 20 | INT 16 | WIS 18 | CHA 23\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Sphinx\n\nImunidades: psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nInscrutable\n\nThe sphinx is immune to any effect that would sense its emotions or read its thoughts, as well as any divination spell that it refuses. Wisdom (Insight) checks made to ascertain the sphinx's intentions or sincerity have disadvantage.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe sphinx's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sphinx makes two claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nRoar (3/Day)\n\nThe sphinx emits a magical roar. Each time it roars before finishing a long rest, the roar is louder and the effect is different, as detailed below. Each creature within 500 feet of the sphinx and able to hear the roar must make a saving throw.\n\n• First Roar\n\n• Second Roar\n\n• Third Roar\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw Attack\n\nThe sphinx makes one claw attack.\n\nTeleport (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe sphinx magically teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.\n\nCast a Spell (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe sphinx casts a spell from its list of prepared spells, using a spell slot as normal."},
  ["creature.angel.psk2014"]={title="Angel",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.angel.psz2014"]={title="Angel",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.angel-of-amonkhet.psa2014"]={title="Angel of Amonkhet",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["deity.angharradh.mtf2014"]={title="Angharradh",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43"},
  ["deity.angharradh.scag2014"]={title="Angharradh",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 23"},
  ["creature.angry-sorrowsworn.mpmm2014"]={title="Angry Sorrowsworn",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 222\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 255 (30d8 + 120)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 10 | CON 19 | INT 8 | WIS 13 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTwo Heads\n\nThe sorrowsworn has advantage on saving throws against being blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, stunned, or knocked unconscious.\n\nRising Anger\n\nIf another creature deals damage to the sorrowsworn, the sorrowsworn's attack rolls have advantage until the end of its next turn, and the first time it hits with a Hook attack on its next turn, the attack's target takes an extra 19 (3d12) psychic damage.\n\nOn its turn, the sorrowsworn has disadvantage on attack rolls if no other creature has dealt damage to it since the end of its last turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sorrowsworn makes two Hook attacks.\n\nHook\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (2d12 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.anhkolox.dsotdq2014"]={title="Anhkolox",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / H\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 157 (15d12 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 11 | CON 18 | INT 4 | WIS 14 | CHA 2\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe anhkolox doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe anhkolox makes two Claw attacks and one Entrapping Rend attack.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 18 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 20 feet in a horizontal direction of the anhkolox's choice.\n\nEntrapping Rend\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h23 (5d6 + 6) piercing damage, and if the target is a Large or smaller creature, the target must succeed on a 18 Strength saving throw or be trapped in the anhkolox's rib cage and grappled (escape 18). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the anhkolox can't use Entrapping Rend on another target."},
  ["spell.animal-friendship.phb2014"]={title="Animal Friendship",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\nThis spell lets you convince a beast that you mean it no harm. Choose a beast that you can see within range. It must see and hear you. If the beast's Intelligence is 4 or higher, the spell fails. Otherwise, the beast must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be charmed by you for the spell's duration. If you or one of your companions harms the target, the spell ends."},
  ["spell.animal-friendship.xphb2024"]={title="Animal Friendship",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 239\n\nTarget a Beast that you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the XPHB condition for the duration. If you or one of your allies deals damage to the target, the spell ends."},
  ["creature.animal-lord.xmm2024"]={title="Animal Lord",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 15\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / M\n\nCR: 20\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 323 (34d8 + 170)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, fly: 60, swim: 60\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 25 | CON 20 | INT 19 | WIS 23 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, necrotic, psychic, radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, stunned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAnimal Lordship\n\nAn animal lord represents a Forager, Hunter, or Sage (DM's choice), which determines certain traits in this stat block.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the animal lord fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nLordly Presence\n\nwis 20, any enemy that starts its turn in a 30-foot XPHB originating from the animal lord. actSaveFail The target suffers one of the following effects:\n\n• Captivated (Forager Only) The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. While XPHB, the target has the XPHB condition.\n\n• Fearful (Hunter Only) The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn.\n\n• Mired (Sage Only) The target takes 10 (3d6) Psychic damage, and the target is magically bewildered until the end of its next turn. While bewildered, the target subtracts 1d4 from its saving throws.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe animal lord has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe animal lord makes two attacks, using Rend or Radiant Ray in any combination, and uses Animal Spirit.\n\nRend\n\nm 13, reach 5 ft. h14 (2d6 + 7) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Force damage.\n\nRadiant Ray\n\nr 12, range 120 ft. h20 (4d6 + 6) Radiant damage.\n\nAnimal Spirit\n\nThe animal lord conjures an animal spirit that strikes at a creature and then disappears. dex 20, one creature the animal lord can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 28 (4d10 + 6) Radiant damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage. actSaveSuccessOrFail One of the following effects occurs:\n\n• Fortify (Forager Only) The animal lord gains 20 XPHB.\n\n• Marked as Prey (Hunter Only) The animal lord has XPHB on attack rolls against the target until the start of the animal lord's next turn.\n\n• Pesky Swarm (Sage Only) The target has XPHB on attack rolls and ability checks until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShape-Shift\n\nThe animal lord shape-shifts into a Huge or smaller version of the animal it represents or a Medium or Small Humanoid, or it returns to its true form. Its game statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nFeral Strike\n\nThe animal lord moves up to its XPHB without provoking XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack.\n\nRadiant Strike\n\nThe animal lord makes one Radiant Ray attack."},
  ["spell.animal-messenger.phb2014"]={title="Animal Messenger",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\nBy means of this spell, you use an animal to deliver a message. Choose a Tiny beast you can see within range, such as a squirrel, a blue jay, or a bat. You specify a location, which you must have visited, and a recipient who matches a general description, such as \"a man or woman dressed in the uniform of the town guard\" or \"a red-haired dwarf wearing a pointed hat.\" You also speak a message of up to twenty-five words. The target beast travels for the duration of the spell toward the specified location, covering about 50 miles per 24 hours for a flying messenger, or 25 miles for other animals.\n\nWhen the messenger arrives, it delivers your message to the creature that you described, replicating the sound of your voice. The messenger speaks only to a creature matching the description you gave. If the messenger doesn't reach its destination before the spell ends, the message is lost, and the beast makes its way back to where you cast this spell."},
  ["spell.animal-messenger.xphb2024"]={title="Animal Messenger",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\nA bestiary of your choice that you can see within range must succeed on a Charisma saving throw, or it attempts to deliver a message for you (if the target's XPHB isn't 0, it automatically succeeds). You specify a location you have visited and a recipient who matches a general description, such as \"a person dressed in the uniform of the town guard\" or \"a red-haired dwarf wearing a pointed hat.\" You also communicate a message of up to twenty-five words. The Beast travels for the duration toward the specified location, covering about 25 miles per 24 hours or 50 miles if the Beast can fly.\n\nWhen the Beast arrives, it delivers your message to the creature that you described, mimicking your communication. If the Beast doesn't reach its destination before the spell ends, the message is lost, and the Beast returns to where you cast the spell."},
  ["spell.animal-shapes.phb2014"]={title="Animal Shapes",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\nYour magic turns others into beasts. Choose any number of willing creatures that you can see within range. You transform each target into the form of a bestiary. On subsequent turns, you can use your action to transform affected creatures into new forms.\n\nThe transformation lasts for the duration for each target, or until the target drops to 0 hit points or dies. You can choose a different form for each target. A target's game statistics are replaced by the statistics of the chosen beast, though the target retains its alignment and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores. The target assumes the hit points of its new form, and when it reverts to its normal form, it returns to the number of hit points it had before it transformed. If it reverts as a result of dropping to 0 hit points, any excess damage carries over to its normal form. As long as the excess damage doesn't reduce the creature's normal form to 0 hit points, it isn't knocked unconscious. The creature is limited in the actions it can perform by the nature of its new form, and it can't speak or cast spells.\n\nThe target's gear melds into the new form. The target can't activate, wield, or otherwise benefit from any of its equipment."},
  ["spell.animal-shapes.xphb2024"]={title="Animal Shapes",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\nChoose any number of willing creatures that you can see within range. Each target shape-shifts into a Large or smaller Beast of your choice that has a XPHB of 4 or lower. You can choose a different form for each target. On later turns, you can take a XPHB action to transform the targets again.\n\nA target's game statistics are replaced by the chosen Beast's statistics, but the target retains its creature type; XPHB; XPHB; alignment; ability to communicate; and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores. The target's actions are limited by the Beast form's anatomy, and it can't cast spells. The target's equipment melds into the new form, and the target can't use any of that equipment while in that form.\n\nThe target gains a number of XPHB equal to the XPHB of the first form into which it shape-shifts. These XPHB vanish if any remain when the spell ends. The transformation lasts for the duration or until the target ends it as a XPHB."},
  ["feature.animal-speaker.xphb2024.barbarian.wild-heart.3"]={title="Animal Speaker",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 55\n\nYou can cast the XPHB and XPHB spells but only as Rituals. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for them."},
  ["spell.animate-dead.phb2014"]={title="Animate Dead",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\nThis spell creates an undead servant. Choose a pile of bones or a corpse of a Medium or Small humanoid within range. Your spell imbues the target with a foul mimicry of life, raising it as an undead creature. The target becomes a skeleton if you chose bones or a zombie if you chose a corpse (the DM has the creature's game statistics).\n\nOn each of your turns, you can use a bonus action to mentally command any creature you made with this spell if the creature is within 60 feet of you (if you control multiple creatures, you can command any or all of them at the same time, issuing the same command to each one). You decide what action the creature will take and where it will move during its next turn, or you can issue a general command, such as to guard a particular chamber or corridor. If you issue no commands, the creature only defends itself against hostile creatures. Once given an order, the creature continues to follow it until its task is complete.\n\nThe creature is under your control for 24 hours, after which it stops obeying any command you've given it. To maintain control of the creature for another 24 hours, you must cast this spell on the creature again before the current 24-hour period ends. This use of the spell reasserts your control over up to four creatures you have animated with this spell, rather than animating a new one."},
  ["spell.animate-dead.xphb2024"]={title="Animate Dead",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\nChoose a pile of bones or a corpse of a Medium or Small Humanoid within range. The target becomes an Undead creature: a XMM if you chose bones or a XMM if you chose a corpse.\n\nOn each of your turns, you can take a XPHB to mentally command any creature you made with this spell if the creature is within 60 feet of you (if you control multiple creatures, you can command any of them at the same time, issuing the same command to each one). You decide what action the creature will take and where it will move on its next turn, or you can issue a general command, such as to guard a chamber or corridor. If you issue no commands, the creature takes the XPHB action and moves only to avoid harm. Once given an order, the creature continues to follow it until its task is complete.\n\nThe creature is under your control for 24 hours, after which it stops obeying any command you've given it. To maintain control of the creature for another 24 hours, you must cast this spell on the creature again before the current 24-hour period ends. This use of the spell reasserts your control over up to four creatures you have animated with this spell rather than animating a new creature."},
  ["spell.animate-objects.phb2014"]={title="Animate Objects",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\nObjects come to life at your command. Choose up to ten nonmagical objects within range that are not being worn or carried. Medium targets count as two objects, Large targets count as four objects, Huge targets count as eight objects. You can't animate any object larger than Huge. Each target animates and becomes a creature under your control until the spell ends or until reduced to 0 hit points.\n\nAs a bonus action, you can mentally command any creature you made with this spell if the creature is within 500 feet of you (if you control multiple creatures, you can command any or all of them at the same time, issuing the same command to each one). You decide what action the creature will take and where it will move during its next turn, or you can issue a general command, such as to guard a particular chamber or corridor. If you issue no commands, the creature only defends itself against hostile creatures. Once given an order, the creature continues to follow it until its task is complete.\n\nSize | HP | AC | Attack | Str | Dex\n\nphb | 20 | 18 | +8 to hit, 1d4 + 4 damage | 4 | 18\n\nphb | 25 | 16 | +6 to hit, 1d8 + 2 damage | 6 | 14\n\nphb | 40 | 13 | +5 to hit, 2d6 + 1 damage | 10 | 12\n\nphb | 50 | 10 | +6 to hit, 2d10 + 2 damage | 14 | 10\n\nphb | 80 | 10 | +8 to hit, 2d12 + 4 damage | 18 | 6\n\nAn animated object is a construct with AC, hit points, attacks, Strength, and Dexterity determined by its size. Its Constitution is 10 and its Intelligence and Wisdom are 3, and its Charisma is 1. Its speed is 30 feet; if the object lacks legs or other appendages it can use for locomotion, it instead has a flying speed of 30 feet and can hover. If the object is securely attached to a surface or a larger object, such as a chain bolted to a wall, its speed is 0. It has blindsight with a radius of 30 feet and is blind beyond that distance. When the animated object drops to 0 hit points, it reverts to its original object form, and any remaining damage carries over to its original object form.\n\nIf you command an object to attack, it can make a single melee attack against a creature within 5 feet of it. It makes a slam attack with an attack bonus and bludgeoning damage determined by its size. The DM might rule that a specific object inflicts slashing or piercing damage based on its form."},
}
